data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T18:52:02.376803+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_041054051c41", "message_id": "msg_asst_f80e8e6df00b", "part_id": "part_6fc8c51d6c5a", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "Let me analyze this carefully.\n\nThe user has already completed the `geospatial` stage, which resolved \"Los Angeles\" to coordinates and a region (center_lat: 34.0536909, center_lon: -118.242766, radius_km: 50).\n\nThe request is: \"Find the nearest EarthScope GNSS station to Los Angeles, stage its time-series CSV, profile it, and create a displacement time-series plot.\"\n\nThis is a **full pipeline request**:\n1. \u2705 Find/resolve the geography: DONE (geospatial)\n2. \u23f3 Find nearest station & stage its CSV: NEEDS `data`\n3. \u23f3 Profile the staged CSV: NEEDS `analysis`\n4. \u23f3 Create a plot: NEEDS `visualization`\n5. \u23f3 Synthesize the answer: NEEDS `synthesis`\n\nAccording to the workflow state:\n- `orchestration_stage`: \"initialized\"\n- `pipeline_required`: [\"geospatial\", \"data\", \"analysis\", \"visualization\", \"synthesis\"]\n- `request_scope`: \"full_pipeline\"\n- Already run: ['geospatial']\n- Not yet run: ['analysis', 'data', 'synthesis', 'visualization']\n\nThe instructions are clear:\n- Route through ONLY the pipeline stages the current request needs\n- The request asks to: FIND \u2192 STAGE \u2192 PROFILE \u2192 PLOT \u2192 explain\n- This is a full study, so run the whole pipeline\n- Start with `data` (now that geospatial is complete)\n- Then `analysis` (profile the staged CSV)\n- Then `visualization` (create a plot)\n- Then `synthesis` (write the final answer)\n\nThe geospatial expert returned:\n- status: resolved\n- region_name: Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\n- center_lat: 34.0536909\n- center_lon: -118.242766\n- radius_km: 50\n- confidence: high\n\nNow I need to route to `data` with these coordinates to discover and stage the nearest GNSS station. The geospatial resolution is complete with high confidence, so I can proceed directly to the data discovery phase to find EarthScope GNSS stations within the 50 km radius around Los Angeles.\n\nThe next step is to query for stations near (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W), identify which one is closest, and retrieve its displacement time-series CSV containing east, north, and up components. Once that data is staged, I'll move through analysis, visualization, and synthesis in sequence."}}

