id: 784
data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T18:53:12.240120+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_041054051c41", "message_id": "msg_asst_f80e8e6df00b", "part_id": "part_faade7365403", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "Let me analyze what's happening here:\n\n1. I've been given a system prompt that says I need to follow an EXACT three-step sequence\n2. Step 1: Search for earthscope/converted datasets - DONE (already in trajectory)\n3. Step 2: Stage the catalog by URL - DONE (already in trajectory)\n4. Step 3: Normalize with shell_bash to keep only first 3 columns\n\nLooking at the trajectory:\n- observation_0 shows the search found the earthscope_stations dataset with the earthscope_converted_data.csv resource\n- observation_1 shows the file was successfully staged to: `D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\earthscope_converted_data.csv`\n\nThe raw file path from the observation is:\n`D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\earthscope_converted_data.csv`\n\nNow I need to do STEP 3: run the shell_bash command to clean the CSV by keeping only columns 1-3.\n\nThe instructions say:\n```\n{ \\\"tool\\\": \\\"shell_bash\\\", \\\"arguments\\\": { \\\"command\\\": \\\"cut -d, -f1-3 '<RAW>' > '<WORKSPACE>/earthscope_stations_clean.csv'\\\" } }\n```\n\nWhere:\n- `<RAW>` = the local_path from step 2 = `D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\earthscope_converted_data.csv`\n- `<WORKSPACE>` = the Active workspace root = `D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace`\n\nThe command should be:\n```\ncut -d, -f1-3 'D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\earthscope_converted_data.csv' > 'D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv'\n```\n\nI need to properly escape the backslashes in the JSON string since each backslash requires escaping as `\\\\`. The final command in JSON format will have doubled backslashes to represent the Windows path correctly. Once this executes, I'll update the workflow_state with the acquisition metadata.\n\nmetadata_path pointing to the cleaned output file at `D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv`, include all required fields from the example, and invoke `finish`.\n\n```"}}

