owerShell parse error\u2014it doesn't recognize the `cut` syntax. I need to use a PowerShell-native approach instead.\n\nI'll use a pipeline combining `Get-Content`, `ForEach-Object`, and `Set-Content` to split each line by comma and keep only the first three fields (station ID and the two coordinate columns). The `-split ','` operator splits each line into an array, `[0..2]` extracts the first three elements (indices 0, 1, 2), and `-join ','` recombines them with commas. This achieves the same result as `cut -d, -f1-3`.", "tool_name_3": "shell_bash", "tool_args_3": {"command": "Get-Content 'D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\earthscope_converted_data.csv' | ForEach-Object {($_ -split ',')[0..2] -join ','} | Set-Content 'D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv'"}, "observation_3": "{\"command\": \"Get-Content 'D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\earthscope_converted_data.csv' | ForEach-Object {($_ -split ',')[0..2] -join ','} | Set-Content 'D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv'\", \"cwd\": \"D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\clio-agent\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"stdout\": \"\", \"stderr\": \"\", \"timed_out\": false, \"timeout_s\": 5.0, \"stdout_truncated\": false, \"stderr_truncated\": false}", "thought_4": "All three required steps have been completed successfully:\n\n1. **STEP 1 (search)** - Located the `earthscope_stations` dataset with `earthscope_converted_data.csv` resource via search terms `[\"earthscope\", \"converted\"]`\n2. **STEP 2 (stage)** - Downloaded the raw CSV to the Active workspace root at `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\earthscope_converted_data.csv` (153 KB)\n3. **STEP 3 (clean)** - Executed PowerShell pipeline to extract first three columns (station ID and two coordinate columns) into `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv`, removing header ambiguity from duplicate \"(deg)\" labels\n\nThe cleaned metadata catalog is ready for the downstream `earthscope_station_catalog` ranker to load and identify stations within 50 km of the Los Angeles center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W). The `acquisition.metadata_path` is now set to the cleaned workspace file as required.", "tool_name_4": "finish", "tool_args_4": {}, "observation_4": "Completed."}, "reasoning": "Successfully executed the three-step EarthScope station metadata discovery sequence as specified:\n\n**STEP 1 (Search):** Queried NDP with search_terms [\"earthscope\", \"converted\"] and located the `earthscope_stations` dataset (ID: 811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41) containing the resource `earthscope_converted_data.csv`.\n\n**STEP 2 (Stage):** Downloaded the raw CSV (153 KB) to the Active workspace root at `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\earthscope_converted_data.csv` using the resource download URL.\n\n**STEP 3 (Clean):** Executed PowerShell pipeline to normalize the raw catalog by extracting only the first three columns (station ID and two coordinate columns) into `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv`. This removes the header ambiguity caused by duplicate \"(deg)\" column name labels in the raw file, preparing clean metadata for downstream station ranking against the Los Angeles region (center 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W, 50 km radius).\n\nThe cleaned metadata catalog is now staged and ready for the earthscope_station_catalog ranker to identify nearby stations."}}}

