data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T18:55:45.674255+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_c2a03e78400244c6", "event_type": "react.step.completed", "session_id": "sess_a6b75b5c73dd", "workspace_id": "ws_ndp_demo", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_041054051c41", "turn_id": "msg_user_041054051c41", "span_id": "sem_c2a03e78400244c6", "parent_span_id": "5d130139536a42b6", "status": "completed", "summary": "earthscope_station_catalog ReAct step 1: geo_filter_points_by_radius", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T18:55:45.534079+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "earthscope_station_catalog", "role": "expert"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {}, "provider": {}, "payload": {"expert_id": "earthscope_station_catalog", "expert_span_id": "5d130139536a42b6", "step_span_id": "6cd48d1aeeeb4678", "step_index": 1, "thought": "Perfect. I can now see the CSV structure clearly:\n- Column 1: `Site` \u2014 the station identifier (e.g., `7ODM`, `ACSB`)\n- Column 2: `Latitude` \u2014 latitude values (34.11640827, 33.27426630, 34.59428106) fall within [-90, 90] and cluster near the LA center (34.0536909\u00b0N) \u2713\n- Column 3: `(deg)` \u2014 despite its odd header name, the values (-117.09319697, -117.44489491, -116.42938185) are clearly longitudes in [-180, 180] range near the LA center (-118.242766\u00b0W) \u2713\n\nThis is exactly the kind of messy header the system rules warn about\u2014`(deg)` is an ambiguous column name, but the VALUES confirm it holds longitude data. I'll pass explicit `lat_column=\"Latitude\"`, `lon_column=\"(deg)\"`, and `id_column=\"Site\"` to ensure robust parsing.\n\nNow I'll call `geo_filter_points_by_radius` with the resolved LA center and 50 km radius to rank all in-region stations by distance.", "reasoning": "", "tool_name": "geo_filter_points_by_radius", "tool_args": {"data_path": "D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\earthscope_stations_cl