, {\"Site\": \"CMP9\", \"Latitude\": \"34.35318168\", \"(deg)\": \"-118.41143044\", \"distance_km\": 36.737, \"id\": \"CMP9\"}, {\"Site\": \"CBHS\", \"Latitude\": \"34.13856359\", \"(deg)\": \"-118.62981150\", \"distance_km\": 36.8677, \"id\": \"CBHS\"}, {\"Site\": \"SPMS\", \"Latitude\": \"33.99265586\", \"(deg)\": \"-117.84878096\", \"distance_km\": 36.9384, \"id\": \"SPMS\"}, {\"Site\": \"CHIL\", \"Latitude\": \"34.33342432\", \"(deg)\": \"-118.02600479\", \"distance_km\": 36.9456, \"id\": \"CHIL\"}, {\"Site\": \"SPK1\", \"Latitude\": \"34.05934504\", \"(deg)\": \"-118.64616754\", \"distance_km\": 37.1681, \"id\": \"SPK1\"}, {\"Site\": \"PVE3\", \"Latitude\": \"33.74329893\", \"(deg)\": \"-118.40426170\", \"distance_km\": 37.595, \"id\": \"PVE3\"}, {\"Site\": \"VTIS\", \"Latitude\": \"33.71264237\", \"(deg)\": \"-118.29382931\", \"distance_km\": 38.2147, \"id\": \"VTIS\"}, {\"Site\": \"PSDM\", \"Latitude\": \"34.09176657\", \"(deg)\": \"-117.80709695\", \"distance_km\": 40.3504, \"id\": \"PSDM\"}, {\"Site\": \"CCCS\", \"Latitude\": \"33.86274477\", \"(deg)\": \"-117.86494857\", \"distance_km\": 40.8052, \"id\": \"CCCS\"}, {\"Site\": \"ROCK\", \"Latitude\": \"34.23567681\", \"(deg)\": \"-118.67643707\", \"distance_km\": 44.7468, \"id\": \"ROCK\"}, {\"Site\": \"LORS\", \"Latitude\": \"34.13332851\", \"(deg)\": \"-117.75407557\", \"distance_km\": 45.8632, \"id\": \"LORS\"}, {\"Site\": \"SACY\", \"Latitude\": \"33.74324750\", \"(deg)\": \"-117.89558382\", \"distance_km\": 47.0996, \"id\": \"SACY\"}, {\"Site\": \"SKYB\", \"Latitude\": \"34.43862574\", \"(deg)\": \"-118.47863507\", \"distance_km\": 47.9804, \"id\": \"SKYB\"}, {\"Site\": \"TWMS\", \"Latitude\": \"33.97245635\", \"(deg)\": \"-117.72552630\", \"distance_km\": 48.5225, \"id\": \"TWMS\"}, {\"Site\": \"CLAR\", \"Latitude\": \"34.10992974\", \"(deg)\": \"-117.70881533\", \"distance_km\": 49.5707, \"id\": \"CLAR\"}]}", "thought_2": "Perfect. The geo_filter_points_by_radius tool has completed successfully with complete coverage: 72 stations within the 50 km radius of Los Angeles center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W). The tool correctly identified the Latitude and (deg) columns despite the ambiguous header, and returned zero invalid records (skipped_invalid=0). All 72 stations are ranked by distance, with MTA1 nearest (0.30 km) and CLAR farthest (49.57 km).\n\nI will now emit the final workflow_state with:\n- status=\"ranked\" (72 within-radius candidates found and ranked by distance)\n- station_ids: all 72 station IDs in the distance-sorted order provided by the tool\n- resource_discovery: one ndp_search_datasets query per station for the resolver to execute\n\nThe resolver will use these queries to search for available time-series datasets for each candidate station, starting with the nearest (most relevant) and falling back to alternatives as needed.", "tool_name_2": "finish", "tool_args_2": {}, "observation_2": "Completed."}, "reasoning": "I examined the staged EarthScope station metadata CSV (`earthscope_stations_clean.csv`) and identified its structure: **Site** (station ID, first column), **Latitude**, and **(deg)** (longitude, despite the unusual header name). The column identification was confirmed by inspecting actual values \u2014 latitude values cluster near 34\u00b0N (the LA center) and fall within [-90, 90], while longitude values cluster near -118\u00b0W and fall within [-180, 180], matching the resolved geographic context.\n\nI then called `geo_filter_points_by_radius` with the resolved LA region center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W) and radius 50 km, passing explicit `lat_column=\"Latitude\"`, `lon_column=\"(deg)\"`, and `id_column=\"Site\"` to ensure robust column mapping (as required by RULE 1). The tool successfully scanned all 1,101 rows in the catalog and returned 72 stations falling within the resolved radius, sorted by distance from the center in ascending order. The result shows `skipped_invalid=0`, confirming correct column parsing and no malformed coordinates \u2014 this is positive proof that the filter executed correctly.\n\nThe 72 within-radius candidates are now ranked by distance to the region center (nearest first), with MTA1 closest at 0.30 km and CLAR farthest at 49.57 km. All 72 station IDs are concrete, verified results from the tool's `points` array \u2014 not invented or padded. Each candidate is ready for the downstream resource resolver to execute individual `ndp_search_datasets` queries to locate and stage time-series datasets."}}}

