op-ranked station (MTA1) time-series data with east, north, and up displacement columns. This is the only remaining step needed to fulfill the user's request for the nearest station's displacement CSV.", "status": "running", "execute": true, "source": "agent_next_expert", "parent_id": "data", "pack_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "stage": "delegate.started", "delegation_lifecycle": "sync", "depth": 0, "execution_mode": "blueprint_react", "stream_source": "live"}, "agent_id": "data", "text": "data -> ndp_resource_resolver", "parent_agent": "data", "child_agent": "ndp_resource_resolver", "stage": "delegate.started", "thought": "The workflow has progressed through two of three required child steps:\n\n1. \u2705 **NDP Dataset Discovery** (completed): Staged the EarthScope station metadata catalog CSV at `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv`.\n\n2. \u2705 **EarthScope Station Catalog** (completed): Ranked 72 candidate stations within the 50 km Los Angeles region. MTA1 is the nearest station at 0.30 km from the center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W).\n\n3. \u23f3 **NDP Resource Resolver** (not yet run): The current state shows `acquisition.status=\"metadata_only\"` and `acquisition.analysis_ready=false` because we have only the station METADATA catalog, not yet a staged time-series CSV.\n\nPer the system instructions: \"YOUR BRANCH IS COMPLETE ONLY WHEN `ndp_resource_resolver` HAS STAGED A REAL STATION TIME-SERIES CSV (`acquisition.status=staged`, `acquisition.analysis_ready=true`, a concrete `acquisition.local_path`).\"\n\nThe next required step is to delegate to `ndp_resource_resolver` to stage the top-ranked station (MTA1) time-series data with east, north, and up displacement columns. This is the only remaining step needed to fulfill the user's request for the nearest station's displacement CSV.", "status": "running"}}}

