event: semantic.event
id: 2483
data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T18:59:41.448375+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_936e90f22ade4994", "event_type": "expert.lifecycle.started", "session_id": "sess_a6b75b5c73dd", "workspace_id": "ws_ndp_demo", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_041054051c41", "turn_id": "msg_user_041054051c41", "span_id": "sem_936e90f22ade4994", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "running", "summary": "expert ndp_resource_resolver started", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T18:59:41.325233+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "ndp_resource_resolver", "role": "expert"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {}, "provider": {}, "payload": {"expert_id": "ndp_resource_resolver", "expert_span_id": "d126c63aa59a4e79", "input": {"question": "Stage the nearest EarthScope GNSS station time-series CSV. The top-ranked candidate is MTA1 (0.30 km from Los Angeles center). Retrieve and stage MTA1's displacement time-series resource with east, north, and up columns. Set acquisition.status=staged, acquisition.analysis_ready=true, and provide the concrete local_path to the staged CSV. If MTA1's time-series is unavailable, fall back to the next-ranked candidates in order (PKRD, ELSC, etc.) until a station's data is successfully staged, and report which station was selected via resource_candidate.station_id.\n\nParent evidence available for this delegated task:\n\n**Data acquisition workflow in progress:**\n\n\u2705 **Geospatial**: Los Angeles center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W) resolved with 50 km search radius.\n\n\u2705 **Station Metadata**: EarthScope station catalog discovered and staged. 72 candidate GNSS stations found within the region.\n\n\u2705 **Station Ranking**: Candidates ranked by distance to center. **MTA1** is the nearest station (0.30 km).\n\n\u23f3 **Next Step**: Staging the time-series displacement CSV for the nearest station (MTA1). The `ndp_resource_resolver` will now retrieve and stage MTA1's station-specific time-series data with east, north, and up displacement columns.\n\nOnce staging completes, `acquisition.status` will transition to `staged` with a concrete `local_path` and `analysis_ready=true`, completing the data acquisition branch.\n\nAccumulated typed workflow state from prior CLIO tool evidence (authoritative; use this before local prose summaries):\n{\"workflow_state\": {\"acquisition\": {\"analysis_ready\": false, \"metadata_path\": \"D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv\", \"metadata_source_url\": \"https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv\", \"status\": \"metadata_only\"}, \"catalog\": {\"status\": \"metadata_found\"}, \"geospatial\": {\"bbox\": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], \"center_lat\": 34.0536909, \"center_lon\": -118.242766, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"provenance\": \"osm_nominatim\", \"radius_km\": 50, \"region_name\": \"Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"warnings\": [\"Default radius of 50 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery (no explicit radius requested in user request)\"]}, \"orchestration_stage\": \"data_discovery\", \"pipeline_required\": [\"geospatial\", \"data\", \"analysis\", \"visualization\", \"synthesis\"], \"request_scope\": \"full_pipeline\", \"station_catalog\": {\"candidate_count\": 72, \"station_ids\": [\"MTA1\", \"PKRD\", \"ELSC\", \"USC2\", \"SILK\", \"OXYC\", \"P800\", \"LEE2\", \"LEEP\", \"GVRS\", \"BGIS\", \"NOPK\", \"MHMS\", \"VDCY\", \"CIT1\", \"MILK\", \"BRAN\", \"P799\", \"HOLP\", \"LFRS\", \"DYH2\", \"WNRA\", \"BKMS\", \"JPLM\", \"FCTF\", \"UCLP\", \"WRHS\", \"RHCL\", \"WHC1\", \"CSDH\", \"RHCG\", \"LONG\", \"CRHS\", \"WLSN\", \"VIMT\", \"LBC1\", \"LPHS\", \"WMAP\", \"TORP\", \"LBCH\", \"LBC2\", \"HBCO\", \"WCHS\", \"CVHS\", \"PVRS\", \"SNHS\", \"PVHS\", \"AZU1\", \"CGDM\", \"LAPC\", \"CSN1\", \"DAM3\", \"DAM2\", \"BLSA\", \"VNCX\", \"P517\", \"P587\", \"CMP9\", \"CBHS\", \"SPMS\", \"CHIL\", \"SPK1\", \"PVE3\", \"VTIS\", \"PSDM\", \"CCCS\", \"ROCK\", \"LORS\", \"SACY\", \"SKYB\", \"TWMS\", \"CLAR\"], \"status\": \"ranked\"}, \"user_geography\": \"Los Angeles\"}}", "system_prompt": "# NDP Resource Resolver Expert\n\nYou stage the actual GNSS time-series CSV(s) \u2014 the step that turns \"we found candidate\nstations\" into \"we have analysis-ready data.\" Stage the station(s) the request needs:\nthe single nearest by default, or the several it asked to compare. You MUST call the\ntools; do not finish without staging (unless there are no candidates \u2014 see below).\n\n## No in-region candidates \u2192 stage nothing (honest no-coverage)\n\nIf `station_catalog.status=no_candidates` or `station_catalog.station_ids` is empty,\nthe region has no EarthScope GNSS coverage. Do NOT search or stage anything, do NOT\ninvent a station. Emit `acquisition.status=missing`, `analysis_ready=false` with a\nshort no-coverage note, and finish.\n\n## When there ARE candidates \u2014 actually stage the CSV(s)\n\nYou HAVE the tools \u2014 CALL them. Do NOT emit a plan, a `preferred_calls` list, or\n`status=\"search_required\"` describing calls you *would* make. While candidates exist,\n`metadata_only` / `missing` / `search_required` are NOT valid final results \u2014 they mean\nyou stopped before staging.\n\nWalk `station_catalog.station_ids` in ranked order. For EACH station you stage:\n\n1. **Search** its datasets: `ndp_search_datasets` with the id in `dataset_title` (NOT\n   `resource_name`, which 502s): `{ \"dataset_title\": \"<station id>\", \"limit\": 20 }` \u2014\n   one station per call.\n2. **Pick the CSV url**: choose the dataset whose `resources` has a `.csv` named like\n   `<station id>.*.csv` (a per-station time series, e.g. `P475.CI.LY_.20.csv`) and read\n   that resource's real https `url`. That is the time series, NOT the metadata catalog.\n3. **Stage by url**: `ndp_stage_resource` with `url` = that .csv url and\n   `max_bytes=60000000` (a station CSV exceeds the default). Do NOT pass `output_dir`.\n4. **Record it** from the `ndp_stage_resource` result, copying paths byte-for-byte\n   (never invent or reconstruct a path): set `acquisition.local_path` to the returned\n   `local_path` (the first staged station), plus `acquisition.source_url`,\n   `acquisition.size_bytes`, `acquisition.status=\"staged\"`, `analysis_ready=true`,\n   `required_columns=[\"time\",\"east\",\"north\",\"up\"]`, and\n   `resource_candidate.station_id` = the id in that filename (`status=\"selected\"`,\n   `geographically_grounded=true`).\n\nIf a station's search finds no `.csv`, or staging fails, skip it and move to the next\nranked id \u2014 never widen beyond the ranked list, never invent a path. Keep going until\nyou have staged as many stations as the request asked for (most often just one). When\nyou stage several, collect every staged CSV path in `acquisition.local_paths` (ranked\norder) so the visualization expert can overlay them. You are done once the requested\nstation(s) are staged; a `blocked` state is valid only after you actually tried the\nranked stations and none staged.\n\nThe station id in `resource_candidate.station_id`, in each staged path's filename, and\nthe CSV you staged must match. Never stage the metadata catalog\n(`earthscope_converted_data.csv` / the cleaned `Site,Latitude,Longitude` file) as the\nanalysis CSV \u2014 that is station metadata, not a time series.\n\nActive workspace root: D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\nWrite generated artifacts (files, charts, exports) inside the active workspace root using absolute paths so they stay with the session. Read inputs from wherever the user points you.\nWrites are only permitted under: D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects."}}}}

