data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:00:34.357355+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_041054051c41", "message_id": "msg_asst_f80e8e6df00b", "part_id": "part_065f0a0f1d55", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "Let me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe workflow has progressed as follows:\n1. Initial setup: Los Angeles geospatial center identified with 50 km search radius\n2. 72 candidate GNSS stations discovered, with MTA1 as the nearest (0.30 km)\n3. My task: Stage MTA1's displacement time-series CSV with east, north, up columns\n\nFrom the trajectory:\n- Thought 0: I searched for MTA1's dataset using `ndp_search_datasets` with `{\"dataset_title\": \"MTA1\", \"limit\": 20}`\n- Observation 0: Successfully found the dataset `MTA1.CI.LY_.30` with a CSV resource at `https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- Thought 1: Identified that this is the correct time-series CSV and planned to stage it\n- Tool 1: Called `ndp_stage_resource` with the CSV URL and `max_bytes=60000000`\n- Observation 1: Successfully staged the resource! Got back:\n  - local_path: `D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n  - size_bytes: 50424246\n  - content_type: text/csv\n  - url: (the source URL we provided)\n\nNow I need to respond with the next action. The task is complete:\n- \u2705 MTA1's dataset was found\n- \u2705 The time-series CSV was located\n- \u2705 The CSV was successfully staged to a local path\n- \u2705 We have the concrete local_path: `D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- \u2705 We have the size_bytes: 50424246\n- \u2705 We have the source URL\n\nSince the resource has been successfully staged with all necessary metadata captured, I have everything required to construct the final answer and complete the workflow.\n\nThe staged resource is now accessible at its local path with full metadata including size and source URL. The acquisition status transitions to \"staged\" and analysis_ready becomes true, enabling handoff to the next expert for data visualization and analysis. I should invoke `finish` with an empty arguments dict to conclude this stage. The station identifier in the filename confirms we selected the correct dataset. The time-series data contains the expected columns (time, east, north, up) from EarthScope GNSS observations, and it's now staged locally and ready for analysis. With the resource successfully acquired and marked as analysis_ready, I can proceed to finish this task."}, "replay": true}

