ata is made available via the National Data Platform pilot project.\", \"resources\": [{\"id\": \"2ec8d2ee-2c3a-451c-8515-4e109e911737\", \"url\": \"https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"name\": \"MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"description\": \"EarthScope CSV\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}, {\"id\": \"db766d8d-aaee-41bd-82c8-20fd3ac5bbf8\", \"url\": \"https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/generated_png/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.png\", \"name\": \"MTA1.CI.LY_.30.png\", \"description\": \"Preview image\", \"format\": \"PNG\"}, {\"id\": \"9a6cc25f-c6ba-4511-8338-e8d718939de3\", \"url\": \"https://di.ndp.utah.edu/datasets/339c7577-adb1-4f8b-a1c2-a45ef2db142e\", \"name\": \"Contextual Insight Dashboard\", \"description\": \"Dashboard\", \"format\": \"HTML\"}], \"extras\": {\"affinity_dataset_uuid\": \"9571e3cc-309b-44ee-bb71-28b77784d898\", \"affinity_endpoint_uuids\": \"[\\\"66dd11c0-44e2-48a6-bc02-a2c568c3a5a8\\\"]\", \"affinity_service_uuids\": \"[\\\"3a5562fc-4f8f-4d6a-985e-c6965f02129a\\\", \\\"5bbe2d35-bf69-4232-9462-aab3a56f8be1\\\", \\\"710d3ae5-971d-4946-9f1e-14f3ec2adae8\\\"]\", \"affinity_triplet_uuid\": \"13507868-11d6-45e2-b201-f100c7344ab6\", \"contextual_insight_id\": \"339c7577-adb1-4f8b-a1c2-a45ef2db142e\", \"documentation_links\": \"{\\\"EarthScope GNSS Realtime\\\": \\\"https://www.earthscope.org/data/gnss-realtime/\\\", \\\"GAGE/UNAVCO Data Access Methods\\\": \\\"https://www.unavco.org/data/gps-gnss/data-access-methods/data-access-methods.html\\\", \\\"GAGE GPS/GNSS Data Overview\\\": \\\"https://www.unavco.org/data/gps-gnss/gps-gnss.html\\\"}\", \"end_time\": \"2024-12-12T23:59:47Z\", \"spatial\": \"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"Point\\\",\\\"coordinates\\\":[-118.245498776,34.055218051]}\", \"start_time\": \"2024-12-03T00:00:00Z\", \"temporal\": \"{\\\"startTime\\\": \\\"2024-12-03T00:00:00Z\\\", \\\"endTime\\\": \\\"2024-12-12T23:59:47Z\\\"}\"}}], \"count\": 1, \"total_found\": 1, \"server\": \"global\", \"search_parameters\": {\"search_terms\": null, \"search_keys\": null, \"dataset_name\": null, \"dataset_title\": \"MTA1\", \"owner_org\": null, \"resource_format\": null, \"search_term\": null, \"filter_list\": null, \"limit\": 20}, \"_meta\": {\"tool\": \"search_datasets\", \"status\": \"success\"}}", "thought_1": "Excellent \u2014 the search found MTA1's dataset successfully. The dataset `MTA1.CI.LY_.30` contains the time-series CSV resource at:\n`https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n\nThis is the per-station displacement time series (matching the `<station_id>.*.csv` pattern). The resource format is CSV, which is exactly what we need. Now I will stage this CSV resource using `ndp_stage_resource`, setting `max_bytes=60000000` to accommodate the larger station time-series file (exceeds the default 50 MiB limit). I will not pass `output_dir`, allowing the system to use the default workspace location.", "tool_name_1": "ndp_stage_resource", "tool_args_1": {"url": "https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "max_bytes": 60000000}, "observation_1": "{\"ok\": true, \"local_path\": \"D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"size_bytes\": 50424246, \"content_type\": \"text/csv\", \"url\": \"https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"method\": \"http\", \"_meta\": {\"tool\": \"stage_resource\", \"status\": \"success\"}}", "thought_2": "MTA1's displacement time-series CSV has been successfully staged from the NDP. The resource was retrieved and written to the local workspace at `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv` with size 50,424,246 bytes. The station ID in the filename (MTA1) matches our ranked selection. We have now:\n- \u2705 Located MTA1's dataset in the NDP\n- \u2705 Identified the time-series CSV resource (MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv)\n- \u2705 Successfully staged the resource to the workspace\n- \u2705 Obtained the concrete local_path, source_url, size_bytes, and content_type\n\nAll required information is now available for the workflow state update: `acquisition.status=staged`, `analysis_ready=true`, `resource_candidate.station_id=MTA1`, `acquisition.source_url` and `acquisition.local_path` set from the staging result. The data acquisition phase is complete and ready to transition to the next expert for analysis and visualization.", "tool_name_2": "finish", "tool_args_2": {}, "observation_2": "Completed."}, "reasoning": "I should explain my approach: searched for MTA1's dataset, found the time-series CSV resource, staged it successfully, and now recording the result with proper status and paths.\n\n### [[ ## answer ## ]]\nThis should contain: staged CSV path, selected source URL, size, and any staging blocker (none in this case).\n\n### [[ ## workflow_state ## ]]\nThis must conform to the JSON schema provided. Looking at the schema:\n- `acquisition` should reflect \"staged\" status with the local path, source URL, and file size populated; `analysis_ready` is true since the data is now available for processing\n- `resource_candidate` should show \"selected\" status with `geographically_grounded` as true and the station identifier set to MTA1\n\n### [[ ## next_expert ## ]]\nBased on the instructions, I should route to the Data Analyzer Expert to begin processing the staged GNSS time-series data.\n\n### [[ ## next_task ## ]]\nLeave empty since the current expert's work is complete.\n\nThe workflow_state schema requires specific fields organized by acquisition and resource_candidate sections. For acquisition, I need to set status to \"staged\" with analysis_ready as true, include the local file path and source URL, capture the file size in bytes, and set local_paths to null. For resource_candidate, the status should be \"selected\" with geographically_grounded marked true and the station_id specified as \"MTA1\". While the instructions reference required_columns for time, east, north, and up measurements, this field doesn't exist in the actual schema, so I'll note it separately in the reasoning rather than including it in the JSON structure.\n\nI successfully retrieved and staged MTA1's time-series displacement CSV:\n\n1. **Dataset Search**: Called `ndp_search_datasets` with `dataset_title=\"MTA1\"` and retrieved the EarthScope dataset `MTA1.CI.LY_.30` containing the time-series CSV resource.\n\n2. **Resource Identification**: Extracted the per-station time-series CSV URL from the dataset's resources:\n   - Resource name: `MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv` (matches the `<station_id>.*.csv` pattern)\n   - URL: `https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n\n3. **Staging**: Called `ndp_stage_resource` with `max_bytes=60000000` to accommodate the station's full time-series file (exceeds default limits). Staging completed successfully without errors.\n\n4. **Result**: The CSV was written to the active workspace root at the returned `local_path`, preserving the exact path string as received from the tool result.\n\nMTA1 is now selected and staged as the analysis-ready resource, with the station ID in the filename matching our ranked selection. The data acquisition phase is complete."}}}

