data: {"type": "message.part.added", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:01:00.368195+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_041054051c41", "message_id": "msg_asst_f80e8e6df00b", "stream_source": "live", "part": {"id": "live_handoff_4ba6d4d46f2b", "type": "expert_handoff", "metadata": {"delegate_to": "ndp_resource_resolver", "agent_id": "ndp_resource_resolver", "question": "Stage the nearest EarthScope GNSS station time-series CSV. The top-ranked candidate is MTA1 (0.30 km from Los Angeles center). Retrieve and stage MTA1's displacement time-series resource with east, north, and up columns. Set acquisition.status=staged, acquisition.analysis_ready=true, and provide the concrete local_path to the staged CSV. If MTA1's time-series is unavailable, fall back to the next-ranked candidates in order (PKRD, ELSC, etc.) until a station's data is successfully staged, and report which station was selected via resource_candidate.station_id.", "thought": "The workflow has progressed through two of three required child steps:\n\n1. \u2705 **NDP Dataset Discovery** (completed): Staged the EarthScope station metadata catalog CSV at `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv`.\n\n2. \u2705 **EarthScope Station Catalog** (completed): Ranked 72 candidate stations within the 50 km Los Angeles region. MTA1 is the nearest station at 0.30 km from the center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W).\n\n3. \u23f3 **NDP Resource Resolver** (not yet run): The current state shows `acquisition.status=\"metadata_only\"` and `acquisition.analysis_ready=false` because we have only the station METADATA catalog, not yet a staged time-series CSV.\n\nPer the system instructions: \"YOUR BRANCH IS COMPLETE ONLY WHEN `ndp_resource_resolver` HAS STAGED A REAL STATION TIME-SERIES CSV (`acquisition.status=staged`, `acquisition.analysis_ready=true`, a concrete `acquisition.local_path`).\"\n\nThe next required step is to delegate to `ndp_resource_resolver` to stage the top-ranked station (MTA1) time-series data with east, north, and up displacement columns. This is the only remaining step needed to fulfill the user's request for the nearest station's displacement CSV.", "status": "completed", "execute": true, "source": "agent_next_expert", "parent_id": "data", "pack_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "provider_id": "", "model_id": "", "fallback_warnings": [], "stage": "delegate.completed", "delegation_lifecycle": "sync", "return_to": "data", "depth": 0, "duration_ms": 79624, "execution_mode": "blueprint_react", "input": "Stage the nearest EarthScope GNSS station time-series CSV. The top-ranked candidate is MTA1 (0.30 km from Los Angeles center). Retrieve and stage MTA1's displacement time-series resource with east, north, and up columns. Set acquisition.status=staged, acquisition.analysis_ready=true, and provide the concrete local_path to the staged CSV. If MTA1's time-series is unavailable, fall back to the next-ranked candidates in order (PKRD, ELSC, etc.) until a station's data is successfully staged, and report which station was selected via resource_candidate.station_id.\n\nParent evidence available for this delegated task:\n\n**Data acquisition workflow in progress:**\n\n\u2705 **Geospatial**: Los Angeles center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W) resolved with 50 km search radius.\n\n\u2705 **Station Metadata**: EarthScope station catalog discovered and staged. 72 candidate GNSS stations found within the region.\n\n\u2705 **Station Ranking**: Candidates ranked by distance to center. **MTA1** is the nearest station (0.30 km).\n\n\u23f3 **Next Step**: Staging the time-series displacement CSV for the nearest station (MTA1). The `ndp_resource_resolver` will now retrieve and stage MTA1's station-specific time-series data with east, north, and up displacement columns.\n\nOnce staging completes, `acquisition.status` will transition to `staged` with a concrete `local_path` and `analysis_ready=true`, completi