data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:01:39.712301+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_041054051c41", "message_id": "msg_asst_f80e8e6df00b", "part_id": "part_d29c9361e1a9", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "Let me carefully analyze this complex orchestrator task.\n\n## Understanding the Context\n\nI am the EarthScope Data Acquisition Expert orchestrator. I have three child experts:\n1. `ndp_dataset_discovery` \u2014 searches NDP and stages the EarthScope station metadata catalog\n2. `earthscope_station_catalog` \u2014 ranks station candidates in the region\n3. `ndp_resource_resolver` \u2014 stages the selected station's time-series CSV\n\n## Current State Analysis\n\nLooking at the accumulated typed workflow_state, I can see:\n\n1. **Geospatial** \u2705 \u2014 `status: \"resolved\"` \n   - Region: Los Angeles\n   - Center: 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W\n   - Radius: 50 km\n\n2. **Data Discovery** \u2705 \u2014 `ndp_dataset_discovery` completed\n   - `acquisition.metadata_path`: `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv`\n   - Metadata source URL provided\n\n3. **Catalog Ranking** \u2705 \u2014 `earthscope_station_catalog` completed\n   - `station_catalog.status`: `\"ranked\"`\n   - Found 72 stations within 50 km radius\n   - Top station: MTA1 (0.30 km from center)\n   - `station_ids` array contains all 72 candidates\n\n4. **Resource Staging** \u2705 \u2014 `ndp_resource_resolver` completed\n   - `resource_candidate.station_id`: `\"MTA1\"` (selected)\n   - `acquisition.status`: `\"staged\"` \n   - `acquisition.local_path`: `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n   - `acquisition.analysis_ready`: `true`\n   - Source URL is available with all required columns: time, east, north, up\n\n## Completion Check\n\nAccording to the system prompt, the data branch is complete when state contains `acquisition.status=staged` AND `acquisition.analysis_ready=true` AND a concrete `acquisition.local_path` from `ndp_resource_resolver`. All three conditions are satisfied: status is staged, analysis_ready is true, and the local path points to the MTA1 station CSV file.\n\nAll child experts have finished their work and populated the workflow_state with actual results from their tool calls. I'm verifying against the anti-fabrication rules to ensure nothing has been invented: the station_id MTA1 came from the child's ranking, the local_path and source_url came from ndp_resource_resolver, and the columns were validated by the resolver. Every value in workflow_state traces back to completed child work, not fabrication.\n\nThe task is complete\u2014I discovered 72 GNSS stations within 50 km of LA, ranked them by distance with MTA1 as nearest at 0.30 km, and staged its CSV with the required east, north, up columns. The workflow chain executed successfully: discovery provided metadata, catalog returned ranked station_ids, and resolver staged the selected station's data. I should now route to the next expert. radius of Los Angeles center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W) and ranked them by distance. MTA1 is the nearest at 0.30 km, followed by 71 other candidates.\n\n3. **ndp_resource_resolver** (\u2705 completed): Successfully staged the time-series CSV for the top-ranked station MTA1. The resolver confirmed:\n   - **Station**: MTA1 (0.30 km from Los Angeles center)\n   - **Staged CSV**: `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv` \n   - **File size**: 50.4 MB\n   - **Required columns verified**: time, east, north, up\n   - **Analysis ready**: Yes\n\nThe data branch is now complete. The workflow_state contains all required evidence.\n\nThe resolver has marked the acquisition as staged and confirmed analysis readiness. The selected station MTA1 is documented with its concrete file path, and the full geospatial resolution history\u2014including all 72 ranked candidates\u2014is preserved in the workflow state. The displacement time-series data is prepared for downstream processing. stations identified (MTA1 at 0.30 km is highest priority)\n\n\u2705 **Nearest Station Selected**: **MTA1** (0.30 km from Los Angeles center)\n\n\u2705 **Time-Series CSV Staged**: \n- **Path**: `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- **Source**: `https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- **File Size**: 50,424,246 bytes\n- **Status**: Staged and analysis-ready\n\n\u2705 **Required Columns Verified**: time, east, north, up (GNSS displacement components)\n\nAll three data-acquisition tasks have completed successfully, so the workflow can move forward to analysis. I'll pass through the workflow_state exactly as the children returned it and set `next_expert='finish'` since all required data is staged with verified columns, no blockers remain, and task requirements are satisfied."}}

