data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:02:34.338625+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_041054051c41", "message_id": "msg_asst_f80e8e6df00b", "part_id": "part_5976805125a1", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "Let me analyze this carefully.\n\nThe user request is: \"Find the nearest EarthScope GNSS station to Los Angeles, stage its time-series CSV, profile it, and create a displacement time-series plot.\"\n\nThe workflow has already completed:\n1. **geospatial**: status=completed - Resolved Los Angeles to coordinates (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W) with 50 km radius\n2. **data**: status=completed - Found 72 stations, staged MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv at D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\n\nThe typed workflow_state shows:\n- `acquisition.status = \"staged\"` \u2705\n- The staged CSV has required columns: time, east, north, up \u2705\n- `analysis_ready = true` \u2705\n- All geographic and station discovery evidence is in place\n\nNow, the user request asks for:\n1. \u2705 Find nearest EarthScope GNSS station - DONE (MTA1, 0.30 km away)\n2. \u2705 Stage its time-series CSV - DONE (staged at the local path)\n3. \u274c Profile it - NOT YET DONE (needs `analysis` expert)\n4. \u274c Create a displacement time-series plot - NOT YET DONE (needs `visualization` expert)\n\nThe `pipeline_required` in workflow_state is: `[\"geospatial\", \"data\", \"analysis\", \"visualization\", \"synthesis\"]`\n\nAlready run: ['geospatial', 'data']\nNot yet run: ['analysis', 'synthesis', 'visualization']\n\nAccording to the instructions:\n- The request explicitly asks for a profile (\"profile it\")\n- The request explicitly asks for a plot (\"create a displacement time-series plot\")\n- So I need to run: `analysis` \u2192 `visualization` \u2192 `synthesis`\n  \nThe next step is to route to `analysis` to profile the staged CSV. The workflow_state confirms acquisition.status is \"staged\" with a valid local_path, all required columns are present, and analysis_ready is true\u2014no blockers exist.\n\nSince geospatial and data have completed their work, I need to continue with analysis to profile the staged station CSV. This will generate the profile metrics required before moving to visualization and synthesis.\n\nThe workflow shows that MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv is staged and ready for analysis. I should delegate to the analysis step to profile this data, which will provide the necessary metrics for the subsequent visualization and synthesis stages. A default 50 km radius was applied for regional GNSS station discovery since no explicit radius was specified in the request. The system has identified 72 candidate stations in the Los Angeles area, with MTA1 selected as the primary resource. The full analysis pipeline is required, encompassing geospatial validation, data retrieval, analysis, visualization, and synthesis stages. I need to analyze the staged station data file at D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv to characterize its properties\u2014examining the temporal span, sampling frequency, data availability, and displacement measurements across the three directional components (east, north, vertical). This profile will inform the visualization work downstream.\n\nThe user's request involves four distinct phases: locating the nearest EarthScope station to Los Angeles (completed with MTA1 at 0.30 km), retrieving its time-series data (completed with the staged CSV), profiling that data (still needed), and generating a displacement plot (still needed). The workflow state confirms geospatial and data stages are done with acquisition.status=\"staged\" and analysis_ready=true. Since data acquisition is complete, I should route to the analysis phase rather than finishing. The CSV contains the necessary GNSS columns (time, east, north, up), so analysis can proceed to profile it, followed by visualization for the plot, then synthesis to deliver the final answer. \"WMAP\", \"TORP\", \"LBCH\", \"LBC2\", \"HBCO\", \"WCHS\", \"CVHS\", \"PVRS\", \"SNHS\", \"PVHS\", \"AZU1\", \"CGDM\", \"LAPC\", \"CSN1\", \"DAM3\", \"DAM2\", \"BLSA\", \"VNCX\", \"P517\", \"P587\", \"CMP9\", \"CBHS\", \"SPMS\", \"CHIL\", \"SPK1\", \"PVE3\", \"VTIS\", \"PSDM\", \"CCCS\", \"ROCK\", \"LORS\", \"SACY\", \"SKYB\", \"TWMS\", \"CLAR\"],\n    \"status\": \"ranked\"\n  },\n  \"user_geography\": \"Los Angeles\"\n}\n\nThe expert routing indicates analysis is next. I need to profile the staged CSV file at the specified path to understand its structure, dimensions, and content before proceeding with the full pipeline."}, "replay": true}

