successfully. I have all the information needed to answer the question.\n\nNow I need to extract the time range and calculate the sample cadence. The timestamps are in milliseconds, spanning from 1733184000000 to 1733189070000, which represents approximately 5070 seconds or 84.5 minutes across the 5000 profiled rows. The consecutive sample timestamps confirm a 1-second interval between epochs.\n\nI have all the necessary data gathered: column names and required fields are identified, total row counts established, time range calculated, sample cadence determined, displacement statistics analyzed, uncertainty ranges documented, missing values counted, and data completeness assessed. Now I'll call `finish` to complete the profiling task."}, "replay": true}

