. The first three are displacement measurements, the next three are uncertainty estimates, and the remaining two are metadata fields. All required displacement and uncertainty columns are present with zero null values across the profiled sample.\n\nTime data spans from 1733184000000 to 1733189070000 milliseconds (approximately 84.5 minutes in the 5000-row sample), with consistent 1-second intervals between consecutive measurements. Displacement values show small magnitudes: eastward motion ranges from -0.07 to -0.03 meters, northward from 0.029 to 0.058 meters, and vertical from 0.051 to 0.224 meters. Uncertainty estimates follow similar patterns across all three spatial dimensions. I need to construct the final outputs for this analysis task. The reasoning should explain that the GNSS time-series profiler successfully analyzed the staged file at the specified path, examining the full 250,000-row dataset while profiling a representative 5,000-row sample due to computational constraints. The answer will include the CSV profile with all required fields capturing the error statistics and quality metrics observed. The workflow state needs to follow the schema model to document completion, with the next expert set to 'finish' since the profiling task is concluded and no further analysis steps are needed. The response structure needs to follow the specified format with the complete file path and metadata. I'm organizing the findings into a comprehensive profile that captures the data examination scope, noting that the scan was limited by the row_scan_cap parameter. The JSON schema shows the profiling is complete for the file located at the full path, with the scan_limited flag indicating the 5,000-row limitation. I'll now synthesize all observations\u2014column inventory, row counts, time range, cadence patterns, displacement metrics, uncertainty bounds, data quality flags, and completeness assessment\u2014into a cohesive summary that acknowledges both what was examined and the constraints of the partial sample."}}

