ainty values are descriptive statistics; no explicit noise thresholds or suitability criteria applied\"], \"missing_values\": {\"count\": 0, \"scope\": \"profiled_rows_5000_only\"}, \"rows_profiled\": 5000, \"rows_scanned\": 250000, \"scan_limited\": true, \"status\": \"complete\", \"time_range_profiled_ms\": {\"max\": 1733189070000, \"min\": 1733184000000, \"span_seconds\": 5070}, \"uncertainty_components\": {\"qChannel\": {\"max\": 2411021, \"mean\": 1847152, \"min\": 1314021, \"note\": \"integer codes; no decoded interpretation available\"}, \"sigEE\": {\"max\": 0.035, \"mean\": 0.0334, \"min\": 0.032, \"unit\": \"m\"}, \"sigNN\": {\"max\": 0.036, \"mean\": 0.033, \"min\": 0.032, \"unit\": \"m\"}, \"sigUU\": {\"max\": 0.066, \"mean\": 0.0651, \"min\": 0.062, \"unit\": \"m\"}}}, \"request_scope\": \"full_pipeline\", \"resource_candidate\": {\"geographically_grounded\": true, \"station_id\": \"MTA1\", \"status\": \"selected\"}, \"station_catalog\": {\"candidate_count\": 72, \"station_ids\": [\"MTA1\", \"PKRD\", \"ELSC\", \"USC2\", \"SILK\", \"OXYC\", \"P800\", \"LEE2\", \"LEEP\", \"GVRS\", \"BGIS\", \"NOPK\", \"MHMS\", \"VDCY\", \"CIT1\", \"MILK\", \"BRAN\", \"P799\", \"HOLP\", \"LFRS\", \"DYH2\", \"WNRA\", \"BKMS\", \"JPLM\", \"FCTF\", \"UCLP\", \"WRHS\", \"RHCL\", \"WHC1\", \"CSDH\", \"RHCG\", \"LONG\", \"CRHS\", \"WLSN\", \"VIMT\", \"LBC1\", \"LPHS\", \"WMAP\", \"TORP\", \"LBCH\", \"LBC2\", \"HBCO\", \"WCHS\", \"CVHS\", \"PVRS\", \"SNHS\", \"PVHS\", \"AZU1\", \"CGDM\", \"LAPC\", \"CSN1\", \"DAM3\", \"DAM2\", \"BLSA\", \"VNCX\", \"P517\", \"P587\", \"CMP9\", \"CBHS\", \"SPMS\", \"CHIL\", \"SPK1\", \"PVE3\", \"VTIS\", \"PSDM\", \"CCCS\", \"ROCK\", \"LORS\", \"SACY\", \"SKYB\", \"TWMS\", \"CLAR\"], \"status\": \"ranked\"}, \"user_geography\": \"Los Angeles\"}}", "output": "**Station MTA1 Preliminary Network Suitability Assessment**\n\n**Geographic and Catalog Context:**\n- MTA1 is the selected primary station candidate for Los Angeles region (center: 34.053\u00b0N, \u2212118.243\u00b0W; bounding box: \u2212118.668\u00b0 to \u2212118.155\u00b0 lon, 33.660\u00b0 to 34.337\u00b0 lat).\n- Ranked within a 72-station GNSS catalog including candidates PKRD, ELSC, USC2, SILK, OXYC, and 66 additional stations.\n- Geographic grounding: confirmed.\n\n**Data Profile Summary (Sample-Based):**\n- **File**: 50.4 MB; 250,000 total rows.\n- **Profiling Scope**: 5,000 rows (2% sample-limited cap).\n- **Column Status**: All 8 required columns present (time, east, north, up, sigEE, sigNN, sigUU, qChannel).\n- **Missing Values (Profiled Sample)**: 0 nulls detected across 5,000 rows (scope: profiled rows only; full-file missing-value status not verified).\n\n**Time and Cadence (Sample Observed Only):**\n- Profiled time range: ~5,070 seconds (~84.5 minutes).\n- Cadence observed in sample: ~1 second between consecutive epochs.\n- **Caveat**: Full-file duration, cadence regularity, and gap characteristics not verified.\n\n**Displacement Component Ranges (Profiled 5,000 Rows):**\n- East: \u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m (mean: \u22120.0472 m)\n- North: 0.029 to 0.058 m (mean: 0.0453 m)\n- Up: 0.051 to 0.224 m (mean: 0.1358 m)\n- **Note**: These are descriptive ranges; displacement statistics do not establish signal quality or noise characteristics in isolation.\n\n**Uncertainty Components (Centimeter-Scale):**\n- **sigEE (East)**: 0.032\u20130.035 m (mean: 0.0334 m) \u2014 ~3.3 cm centimeter-scale\n- **sigNN (North)**: 0.032\u20130.036 m (mean: 0.033 m) \u2014 ~3.3 cm centimeter-scale\n- **sigUU (Up)**: 0.062\u20130.066 m (mean: 0.0651 m) \u2014 ~6.5 cm centimeter-scale\n- **qChannel**: 1314021\u20132411021 (integer flag; no decoded interpretation available)\n- **Assessment**: Centimeter-level horizontal and vertical uncertainties are populated. These numeric summaries are not fitness-for-analysis certificates; no explicit noise thresholds or analytical-fitness criteria are applied.\n\n**Network Suitability Determination:**\n- **Single-Station Adequacy**: MTA1 meets data staging and column inventory requirements. Geographic positioning within the Los Angeles region is confirmed. Sample-level data continuity (zero missing values, consistent ~1-second cadence in visible epochs) supports preliminary staging readiness.\n- **Multi-Station Considerations**: Network-level station spacing, coverage gaps, and inter-station cross-validation requirements are not addressed in current evidence. Downstream visualization and synthesis should evaluate whether MTA1 alone provides sufficient spatial coverage or whether a multi-station fanout (e.g., to PKRD, ELSC, USC2) is necessary for regional confidence, network redundancy, or deformation-pattern triangulation.\n\n**Analytical Fitness (Preliminary):**\n- Column inventory: complete.\n- Geographic grounding: confirmed.\n- Centimeter-scale uncertainties: present and quantified (not sub-centimeter).\n- Sample-level continuity: no missing values in profiled 5,000 rows.\n- **Full-file verification pending**: Duration, gap structure, cadence regularity, outlier extent, and complete missing-value assessment require full-file profiling.\n- **Quality assessment**: qChannel numeric range available; decoded interpretation not available. Quality flag status assessed descriptively only.\n\n**Conclusion:**\nMTA1 is a **geographically grounded, preliminary candidate** meeting data inventory and column completeness requirements. Centimeter-scale uncertainty components and sample-observed ~1-second cadence support staging. **Full-file temporal characteristics, noise baselines, and gap-free verification are required for downstream analysis fitness certification.** Network-level integration (distance to PKRD, ELSC, USC2, and others; inter-station spacing) should inform multi-station validation strategy. Current assessment is at the level of column/range review and geographic positioning; further refinement of temporal continuity, analytical fitness, and network coverage fit requires complete-file analysis and comparative station-pair evaluation.", "output_summary": "**Station MTA1 Preliminary Network Suitability Assessment**\n\n**Geographic and Catalog Context:**\n- MTA1 is the selected primary station candidate for Los Angeles region (center: 34.053\u00b0N, \u2212118.243\u00b0W; bounding box: \u2212118.668\u00b0 to \u2212118.155\u00b0 lon, 33.660\u00b0 to 34.337\u00b0 lat).\n- Ranked within a 72-station GNSS catalog including candidates PKRD, ELSC, USC2, SILK, OXYC, and 66 additional stations.\n- Geographic grounding: confirmed.\n\n**Data Profile Summary (Sample-Based):**\n- **File**: 50.4 MB; 250,000 total rows.\n- **Profiling Scope**: 5,000 rows (2% sample-limited cap).\n- **Column Status**: All 8 required columns present (time, east, north, up, sigEE, sigNN, sigUU, qChannel).\n- **Missing Values (Profiled Sample)**: 0 nulls detected across 5,000 rows (scope: profiled rows only; full-file missing-value status not verified).\n\n**Time and Cadence (Sample Observed Only):**\n- Profiled time range: ~5,070 seconds (~84.5 minutes).\n- Cadence observed in sample: ~1 second between consecutive epochs.\n- **Caveat**: Full-file duration, cadence regularity, and gap characteristics not verified.\n\n**Displacement Component Ranges (Profiled 5,000 Rows):**\n- East: \u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m (mean: \u22120.0472 m)\n- North: 0.029 to 0.058 m (mean: 0.0453 m)\n- Up: 0.051 to 0.224 m (mean: 0.1358 m)\n- **Note**: These are descriptive ranges; displacement statistics do not establish signal quality or noise characteristics in isolation.\n\n**Uncertainty Components (Centimeter-Scale):**\n- **sigEE (East)**: 0.032\u20130.035 m (mean: 0.0334 m) \u2014 ~3.3 cm centimeter-scale\n- **sigNN (North)**: 0.032\u20130.036 m (mean: 0.033 m) \u2014 ~3.3 cm centimeter-scale\n- **sigUU (Up)**: 0.062\u20130.066 m (mean: 0.0651 m) \u2014 ~6.5 cm centimeter-scale\n- **qChannel**: 1314021\u20132411021 (integer flag; no decoded interpretation available)\n- **Assessment**: Centimeter-level horizontal and vertical uncertainties are populated. These numeric summaries are not fitness-for-analysis certificates; no explicit noise thresholds or analytical-fitness criteria are applied.\n\n**Network Suitability Determination:**\n- **Single-Station Adequacy**: MTA1 meets data staging and column inventory requirements. Geographic positioning within the Los Angeles region is confirmed. Sample-level data continuity (zero missing values, consistent ~1-second cadence in visible epochs) supports preliminary staging readiness.\n- **Multi-Station Considerations**: Network-level station spacing, coverage gaps, and inter-station cross-validation requirements are not addressed in current evidence. Downstream visualization and synthesis should evaluate whether MTA1 alone provides sufficient spatial coverage or whether a multi-station fanout (e.g., to PKRD, ELSC, USC2) is necessary for regional confidence, network redundancy, or deformation-pattern triangulation.\n\n**Analytical Fitness (Preliminary):**\n- Column inventory: complete.\n- Geographic grounding: confirmed.\n- Centimeter-scale uncertainties: present and quantified (not sub-centimeter).\n- Sample-level continuity: no missing values in profiled 5,000 rows.\n- **Full-file verification pending**: Duration, gap structure, cadence regularity, outlier extent, and complete missing-value assessment require full-file profiling.\n- **Quality assessment**: qChannel numeric range available; decoded interpretation not available. Quality flag status assessed descriptively only.\n\n**Conclusion:**\nMTA1 is a **geographically grounded, preliminary candidate** meeting data inventory and column completeness requirements. Centimeter-scale uncertainty components and sample-observed ~1-second cadence support staging. **Full-file temporal characteristics, noise baselines, and gap-free verification are required for downstream analysis fitness certification.** Network-level integration (distance to PKRD, ELSC, USC2, and others; inter-station spacing) should inform multi-station validation strategy. Current assessment is at the level of column/range review and geographic positioning; further refinement of temporal continuity, analytical fitness, and network coverage fit requires complete-file analysis and comparative station-pair evaluation.", "output_raw": "", "workflow_state": {"acquisition": {"analysis_ready": true, "local_path": "D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "metadata_path": "D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv", "metadata_source_url": "https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv", "size_bytes": 50424246, "source_url": "https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "status": "staged"}, "catalog": {"status": "metadata_found"}, "geospatial": {"bbox": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], "center_lat": 34.0536909, "center_lon": -118.242766, "confidence": "high", "provenance": "osm_nominatim", "radius_km": 50, "region_name": "Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States", "status": "resolved"}, "orchestration_stage": "analysis_complete", "pipeline_required": ["geospatial", "data", "analysis", "visualization", "synthesis"], "profile": {"cadence_observed_seconds": 1, "columns": ["time", "east", "north", "up", "sigEE", "sigNN", "sigUU", "qChannel"], "columns_status": "all_required_present", "displacement_components": {"east": {"max": -0.03, "mean": -0.0472, "min": -0.07, "unit": "m"}, "north": {"max": 0.058, "mean": 0.0453, "min": 0.029, "unit": "m"}, "up": {"max": 0.224, "mean": 0.1358, "min": 0.051, "unit": "m"}}, "limitations": ["Numeric summaries derived from 5,000-row sample (2% of 250,000 total); full-file characteristics not verified", "Time range reflects profiled sample only; full-file duration unknown", "Cadence observed in sample; full-file continuity and gaps not verified", "Missing-value status assessed for profiled rows only; full-file missing-value occurrence unknown", "Uncertainty values are descriptive statistics; no explicit noise thresholds or suitability criteria applied"], "missing_values": {"count": 0, "scope": "profiled_rows_5000_only"}, "rows_profiled": 5000, "rows_scanned": 250000, "scan_limited": true, "status": "complete", "time_range_profiled_ms": {"max": 1733189070000, "min": 1733184000000, "span_seconds": 5070}, "uncertainty_components": {"qChannel": {"max": 2411021, "mean": 1847152, "min": 1314021, "note": "integer codes; no decoded interpretation available"}, "sigEE": {"max": 0.035, "mean": 0.0334, "min": 0.032, "unit": "m"}, "sigNN": {"max": 0.036, "mean": 0.033, "min": 0.032, "unit": "m"}, "sigUU": {"max": 0.066, "mean": 0.0651, "min": 0.062, "unit": "m"}}}, "request_scope": "full_pipeline", "resource_candidate": {"geographically_grounded": true, "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "selected", "network_suitability": {"status": "preliminary", "data_inventory": "complete", "geographic_context": "ranked_primary_in_72_station_catalog", "sample_continuity": "no_missing_values_in_profiled_5000_rows", "cadence_observed_sample": "1_second_not_full_file_verified", "uncertainty_scale": "centimeter_level_3_to_7_cm", "quality_flag_status": "opaque_integer_code_no_interpretation", "full_file_assessment_required": ["duration_verification", "gap_structure", "cadence_regularity", "outlier_analysis", "complete_missing_value_assessment"], "multi_station_validation": "recommended_for_network_coverage_and_cross_check", "next_steps": "complete_file_profiling_and_inter_station_distance_analysis"}}, "station_catalog": {"candidate_count": 72, "station_ids": ["MTA1", "PKRD", "ELSC", "USC2", "SILK", "OXYC", "P800", "LEE2", "LEEP", "GVRS", "BGIS", "NOPK", "MHMS", "VDCY", "CIT1", "MILK", "BRAN", "P799", "HOLP", "LFRS", "DYH2", "WNRA", "BKMS", "JPLM", "FCTF", "UCLP", "WRHS", "RHCL