event: semantic.event
id: 4999
data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:13:07.085985+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_3247f883d23649c5", "event_type": "expert.response.completed", "session_id": "sess_a6b75b5c73dd", "workspace_id": "ws_ndp_demo", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_041054051c41", "turn_id": "msg_user_041054051c41", "span_id": "sem_3247f883d23649c5", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "completed", "summary": "Expert station_network_analysis produced a response.", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:13:06.948398+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "station_network_analysis"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {"agent_blueprint_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "parent_expert": "analysis"}, "provider": {"provider_id": "", "model_id": ""}, "payload": {"selected_expert": "station_network_analysis", "route_source": "agent_blueprint", "route_reason": "Session selected Agent Blueprint expert 'station_network_analysis'.", "answer": "**Station MTA1 Preliminary Network Suitability Assessment**\n\n**Geographic and Catalog Context:**\n- MTA1 is the selected primary station candidate for Los Angeles region (center: 34.053\u00b0N, \u2212118.243\u00b0W; bounding box: \u2212118.668\u00b0 to \u2212118.155\u00b0 lon, 33.660\u00b0 to 34.337\u00b0 lat).\n- Ranked within a 72-station GNSS catalog including candidates PKRD, ELSC, USC2, SILK, OXYC, and 66 additional stations.\n- Geographic grounding: confirmed.\n\n**Data Profile Summary (Sample-Based):**\n- **File**: 50.4 MB; 250,000 total rows.\n- **Profiling Scope**: 5,000 rows (2% sample-limited cap).\n- **Column Status**: All 8 required columns present (time, east, north, up, sigEE, sigNN, sigUU, qChannel).\n- **Missing Values (Profiled Sample)**: 0 nulls detected across 5,000 rows (scope: profiled rows only; full-file missing-value status not verified).\n\n**Time and Cadence (Sample Observed Only):**\n- Profiled time range: ~5,070 seconds (~84.5 minutes).\n- Cadence observed in sample: ~1 second between consecutive epochs.\n- **Caveat**: Full-file duration, cadence regularity, and gap characteristics not verified.\n\n**Displacement Component Ranges (Profiled 5,000 Rows):**\n- East: \u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m (mean: \u22120.0472 m)\n- North: 0.029 to 0.058 m (mean: 0.0453 m)\n- Up: 0.051 to 0.224 m (mean: 0.1358 m)\n- **Note**: These are descriptive ranges; displacement statistics do not establish signal quality or noise characteristics in isolation.\n\n**Uncertainty Components (Centimeter-Scale):**\n- **sigEE (East)**: 0.032\u20130.035 m (mean: 0.0334 m) \u2014 ~3.3 cm centimeter-scale\n- **sigNN (North)**: 0.032\u20130.036 m (mean: 0.033 m) \u2014 ~3.3 cm centimeter-scale\n- **sigUU (Up)**: 0.062\u20130.066 m (mean: 0.0651 m) \u2014 ~6.5 cm centimeter-scale\n- **qChannel**: 1314021\u20132411021 (integer flag; no decoded interpretation available)\n- **Assessment**: Centimeter-level horizontal and vertical uncertainties are populated. These numeric summaries are not fitness-for-analysis certificates; no explicit noise thresholds or analytical-fitness criteria are applied.\n\n**Network Suitability Determination:**\n- **Single-Station Adequacy**: MTA1 meets data staging and column inventory requirements. Geographic positioning within the Los Angeles region is confirmed. Sample-level data continuity (zero missing values, consistent ~1-second cadence in visible epochs) supports preliminary staging readiness.\n- **Multi-Station Considerations**: Network-level station spacing, coverage gaps, and inter-station cross-validation requirements are not addressed in current evidence. Downstream visualization and synthesis should evaluate whether MTA1 alone provides sufficient spatial coverage or whether a multi-station fanout (e.g., to PKRD, ELSC, USC2) is necessary for regional confidence, network redundancy, or deformation-pattern triangulation.\n\n**Analytical Fitness (Preliminary):**\n- Column inventory: complete.\n- Geographic grounding: confirmed.\n- Centimeter-scale uncertainties: present and quantified (not sub-centimeter).\n- Sample-level continuity: no missing values in profiled 5,000 rows.\n- **Full-file verification pending**: Duration, gap structure, cadence regularity, outlier extent, and complete missing-value assessment require full-file profiling.\n- **Quality assessment**: qChannel numeric range available; decoded interpretation not available. Quality flag status assessed descriptively only.\n\n**Conclusion:**\nMTA1 is a **geographically grounded, preliminary candidate** meeting data inventory and column completeness requirements. Centimeter-scale uncertainty components and sample-observed ~1-second cadence support staging. **Full-file temporal characteristics, noise baselines, and gap-free verification are required for downstream analysis fitness certification.** Network-level integration (distance to PKRD, ELSC, USC2, and others; inter-station spacing) should inform multi-station validation strategy. Current assessment is at the level of column/range review and geographic positioning; further refinement of temporal continuity, analytical fitness, and network coverage fit requires complete-file analysis and comparative station-pair evaluation.", "expert_handoffs": [], "tools_called": [], "file_diffs": [], "error_info": null, "reasoning": "The MTA1 time-series profile evaluation requires careful alignment with evidence-based constraints:\n\n1. **Sample-Limited Evidence**: The profile is based on 5,000 rows (2% of 250,000 total). Full-file duration, continuity, gap structure, cadence regularity, and outlier extent cannot be inferred from sample statistics alone. Time range (5,070 seconds, ~84.5 minutes) and cadence (~1 second) reflect the profiled sample only.\n\n2. **Geographic Grounding**: MTA1 is embedded in a ranked 72-station Los Angeles catalog with confirmed region center (34.053\u00b0N, \u2212118.243\u00b0W). MTA1 is designated the selected primary candidate.\n\n3. **Column and Data Inventory**: All 8 required columns present (time, east, north, up, sigEE, sigNN, sigUU, qChannel). Zero missing values in profiled rows; missing-value status in full file unknown. Sample rows show no 1-second cadence gaps in visible epochs, but full-file continuity is not verified.\n\n4. **Uncertainty Scale Clarification**: Uncertainty components (sigEE, sigNN, sigUU) range 0.032\u20130.066 m. These values fall in the centimeter scale (~3\u20137 cm), not sub-centimeter (< 0.01 m = < 1 cm). Uncertainty statistics are descriptive; they do not constitute quality thresholds or suitability certification without explicit criteria.\n\n5. **Opaque Quality Flag**: qChannel (mean 1847152, range 1314021\u20132411021) is an integer code. No decoded interpretation or threshold-based quality assessment is provided. Numeric statistics alone do not justify \"high-quality\" labels.\n\n6. **Network Context**: 72-station catalog includes ranked candidates (PKRD, ELSC, USC2, SILK, and 67 others). Network-level gaps, inter-station distances, and coverage adequacy for multi-station fanout are not yet analyzed. Single-station suitability is geographically grounded; network synthesis fitness requires comparative station-spacing analysis.\n\n7. **Compliance with Constraints**: No claims about Hz, days, continuous behavior, full-record duration, processing software, or reference frames are issued. Assessment remains at column/range review and preliminary geographic positioning level."}}, "replay": true}

