id: 5001
data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:13:07.838022+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_4d1fa81e9c994259", "event_type": "blueprint.delegation.completed", "session_id": "sess_a6b75b5c73dd", "workspace_id": "ws_ndp_demo", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_041054051c41", "turn_id": "msg_user_041054051c41", "span_id": "sem_4d1fa81e9c994259", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "completed", "summary": "**Station MTA1 Preliminary Network Suitability Assessment**\n\n**Geographic and Catalog Context:**\n- MTA1 is the selected primary station candidate for Los Angeles region (center: 34.053\u00b0N, \u2212118.243\u00b0W; bounding box: \u2212118.668\u00b0 to \u2212118.155\u00b0 lon, 33.660\u00b0 to 34.337\u00b0 lat).\n- Ranked within a 72-station GNSS catalog including candidates PKRD, ELSC, USC2, SILK, OXYC, and 66 additional stations.\n- Geographic grounding: confirmed.\n\n**Data Profile Summary (Sample-Based):**\n- **File**: 50.4 MB; 250,000 total rows.\n- **Profiling Scope**: 5,000 rows (2% sample-limited cap).\n- **Column Status**: All 8 required columns present (time, east, north, up, sigEE, sigNN, sigUU, qChannel).\n- **Missing Values (Profiled Sample)**: 0 nulls detected across 5,000 rows (scope: profiled rows only; full-file missing-value status not verified).\n\n**Time and Cadence (Sample Observed Only):**\n- Profiled time range: ~5,070 seconds (~84.5 minutes).\n- Cadence observed in sample: ~1 second between consecutive epochs.\n- **Caveat**: Full-file duration, cadence regularity, and gap characteristics not verified.\n\n**Displacement Component Ranges (Profiled 5,000 Rows):**\n- East: \u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m (mean: \u22120.0472 m)\n- North: 0.029 to 0.058 m (mean: 0.0453 m)\n- Up: 0.051 to 0.224 m (mean: 0.1358 m)\n- **Note**: These are descriptive ranges; displacement statistics do not establish signal quality or noise characteristics in isolation.\n\n**Uncertainty Components (Centimeter-Scale):**\n- **sigEE (East)**: 0.032\u20130.035 m (mean: 0.0334 m) \u2014 ~3.3 cm centimeter-scale\n- **sigNN (North)**: 0.032\u20130.036 m (mean: 0.033 m) \u2014 ~3.3 cm centimeter-scale\n- **sigUU (Up)**: 0.062\u20130.066 m (mean: 0.0651 m) \u2014 ~6.5 cm centimeter-scale\n- **qChannel**: 1314021\u20132411021 (integer flag; no decoded interpretation available)\n- **Assessment**: Centimeter-level horizontal and vertical uncertainties are populated. These numeric summaries are not fitness-for-analysis certificates; no explicit noise thresholds or analytical-fitness criteria are applied.\n\n**Network Suitability Determination:**\n- **Single-Station Adequacy**: MTA1 meets data staging and column inventory requirements. Geographic positioning within the Los Angeles region is confirmed. Sample-level data continuity (zero missing values, consistent ~1-second cadence in visible epochs) supports preliminary staging readiness.\n- **Multi-Station Considerations**: Network-level station spacing, coverage gaps, and inter-station cross-validation requirements are not addressed in current evidence. Downstream visualization and synthesis should evaluate whether MTA1 alone provides sufficient spatial coverage or whether a multi-station fanout (e.g., to PKRD, ELSC, USC2) is necessary for regional confidence, network redundancy, or deformation-pattern triangulation.\n\n**Analytical Fitness (Preliminary):**\n- Column inventory: complete.\n- Geographic grounding: confirmed.\n- Centimeter-scale uncertainties: present and quantified (not sub-centimeter).\n- Sample-level continuity: no missing values in profiled 5,000 rows.\n- **Full-file verification pending**: Duration, gap structure, cadence regularity, outlier extent, and complete missing-value assessment require full-file profiling.\n- **Quality assessment**: qChannel numeric range available; decoded interpretation not available. Quality flag status assessed descriptively only.\n\n**Conclusion:**\nMTA1 is a **geographically grounded, preliminary candidate** meeting data inventory and column completeness requirements. Centimeter-scale uncertainty components and sample-observed ~1-second cadence support staging. **Full-file temporal characteristics, noise baselines, and gap-free verification are required for downstream analysis fitness certification.** Network-level integration (distance to PKRD, ELSC, USC2, and others; inter-station spacing) should inform multi-station validation strategy. Current assessment is at the level of column/range review and geographic positioning; further refinement of temporal continuity, analytical fitness, and network coverage fit requires complete-file analysis and comparative station-pair evaluation.", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:13:07.695825+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "station_network_analysis", "role": "child_expert"}, "subject": {"agent_id": "analysis", "role": "parent_expert"}, "blueprint": {"pack_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "agent_blueprint_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "parent_expert": "analysis", "child_expert": "station_network_analysis"}, "provider": {"provider_id": "", "model_id": ""}, "payload": {"delegate_to": "station_network_analysis", "agent_id": "station_network_analysis", "question": "Assess the suitability and network context of station MTA1 based on the completed profile of MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv (50.4 MB; 250,000 rows; all 8 required columns present; 5,000-row sample profiled with scan-limited statistics available: ~1 second cadence observed, displacement ranges profiled, uncertainty components present, zero nulls in sample). Evaluate MTA1's network positioning, station spacing, coverage, and analytical fitness within the Los Angeles region's 72-station GNSS catalog (including ranked candidates: MTA1, PKRD, ELSC, USC2, SILK, and others). Provide network-level suitability assessment to support downstream visualization and synthesis.", "thought": "The `gnss_timeseries_analysis` child has completed profile analysis of the staged MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv file (50.4 MB, 250,000 rows). The profile confirms all required columns are present and properly typed. Key profiled-sample findings include:\n\n- **Columns:** time (ms epoch), east/north/up displacement (m), sigEE/sigNN/sigUU uncertainty (m), qChannel quality flag (integer)\n- **Profile scope:** 5,000 rows profiled (2% sample cap); full-file statistics not verified\n- **Time span (sample):** ~5,070 seconds (~84.5 minutes)\n- **Cadence (sample):** ~1 second observed\n- **Displacements (sample):** east [\u22120.07, \u22120.03 m], north [0.029, 0.058 m], up [0.051, 0.224 m]\n- **Uncertainties (sample):** sigEE/sigNN ~0.033 m mean, sigUU ~0.065 m mean\n- **Completeness (sample):** 0 nulls in 5,000 rows\n\nCritical caveat: All statistics, time range, cadence, and completeness assessments are restricted to the profiled sample. Full-file duration, continuity, gaps, and complete missing-value status have not been verified.\n\nThe user's request specifies this profile \"supports downstream visualization and final answer synthesis\" with `request_scope: \"full_pipeline\"`. The required pipeline is `[\"geospatial\", \"data\", \"analysis\", \"visualization\", \"synthesis\"]`. Geospatial (\u2713) and data staging (\u2713) are complete. Analysis is in progress: gnss_timeseries_analysis (\u2713 done), seismic_event_catalog (not requested\u2014user asked only for time-series profile, not earthquakes), station_network_analysis (not yet run\u2014required to complete the analysis phase).\n\n**Next step:** Delegate to `station_network_analysis` to assess MTA1's suitability and network context in the Los Angeles region's 72-station catalog, then finish with comprehensive analysis synthesis.", "status": "completed", "execute": true, "source": "agent_next_expert", "parent_id": "analysis", "pack_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "provider_id": "", "model_id": "", "fallback_warnings": [], "stage": "