TA1 meets data staging and column inventory requirements. Geographic positioning within the Los Angeles region is confirmed. Sample-level data continuity (zero missing values, consistent ~1-second cadence in visible epochs) supports preliminary staging readiness.\n- **Multi-Station Considerations**: Network-level station spacing, coverage gaps, and inter-station cross-validation requirements are not addressed in current evidence. Downstream visualization and synthesis should evaluate whether MTA1 alone provides sufficient spatial coverage or whether a multi-station fanout (e.g., to PKRD, ELSC, USC2) is necessary for regional confidence, network redundancy, or deformation-pattern triangulation.\n\n**Analytical Fitness (Preliminary):**\n- Column inventory: complete.\n- Geographic grounding: confirmed.\n- Centimeter-scale uncertainties: present and quantified (not sub-centimeter).\n- Sample-level continuity: no missing values in profiled 5,000 rows.\n- **Full-file verification pending**: Duration, gap structure, cadence regularity, outlier extent, and complete missing-value assessment require full-file profiling.\n- **Quality assessment**: qChannel numeric range available; decoded interpretation not available. Quality flag status assessed descriptively only.\n\n**Conclusion:**\nMTA1 is a **geographically grounded, preliminary candidate** meeting data inventory and column completeness requirements. Centimeter-scale uncertainty components and sample-observed ~1-second cadence support staging. **Full-file temporal characteristics, noise baselines, and gap-free verification are required for downstream analysis fitness certification.** Network-level integration (distance to PKRD, ELSC, USC2, and others; inter-station spacing) should inform multi-station validation strategy. Current assessment is at the level of column/range review and geographic positioning; further refinement of temporal continuity, analytical fitness, and network coverage fit requires complete-file analys