data: {"type": "message.part.added", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:13:07.838022+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_041054051c41", "message_id": "msg_asst_f80e8e6df00b", "stream_source": "live", "part": {"id": "live_handoff_dd96b0d37451", "type": "expert_handoff", "metadata": {"delegate_to": "station_network_analysis", "agent_id": "station_network_analysis", "question": "Assess the suitability and network context of station MTA1 based on the completed profile of MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv (50.4 MB; 250,000 rows; all 8 required columns present; 5,000-row sample profiled with scan-limited statistics available: ~1 second cadence observed, displacement ranges profiled, uncertainty components present, zero nulls in sample). Evaluate MTA1's network positioning, station spacing, coverage, and analytical fitness within the Los Angeles region's 72-station GNSS catalog (including ranked candidates: MTA1, PKRD, ELSC, USC2, SILK, and others). Provide network-level suitability assessment to support downstream visualization and synthesis.", "thought": "The `gnss_timeseries_analysis` child has completed profile analysis of the staged MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv file (50.4 MB, 250,000 rows). The profile confirms all required columns are present and properly typed. Key profiled-sample findings include:\n\n- **Columns:** time (ms epoch), east/north/up displacement (m), sigEE/sigNN/sigUU uncertainty (m), qChannel quality flag (integer)\n- **Profile scope:** 5,000 rows profiled (2% sample cap); full-file statistics not verified\n- **Time span (sample):** ~5,070 seconds (~84.5 minutes)\n- **Cadence (sample):** ~1 second observed\n- **Displacements (sample):** east [\u22120.07, \u22120.03 m], north [0.029, 0.058 m], up [0.051, 0.224 m]\n- **Uncertainties (sample):** sigEE/sigNN ~0.033 m mean, sigUU ~0.065 m mean\n- **Completeness (sample):** 0 nulls in 5,000 rows\n\nCritical caveat: All statistics, time range, cadence, and completeness assessments are restricted to the profiled sample. Full-file duration, continuity, gaps, and complete missing-value status have not been verified.\n\nThe user's request specifies this profile \"supports downstream visualization and final answer synthesis\" with `request_scope: \"full_pipeline\"`. The required pipeline is `[\"geospatial\", \"data\", \"analysis\", \"visualization\", \"synthesis\"]`. Geospatial (\u2713) and data staging (\u2713) are complete. Analysis is in progress: gnss_timeseries_analysis (\u2713 done), seismic_event_catalog (not requested\u2014user asked only for time-series profile, not earthquakes), station_network_analysis (not yet run\u2014required to complete the analysis phase).\n\n**Next step:** Delegate to `station_network_analysis` to assess MTA1's suitability and network context in the Los Angeles region's 72-station catalog, then finish with comprehensive analysis synthesis.", "status": "completed", "execute": true, "source": "agent_next_expert", "parent_id": "analysis", "pack_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "provider_id": "", "model_id": "", "fallback_warnings": [], "stage": "delegate.completed", "delegation_lifecycle": "sync", "return_to": "analysis", "depth": 0, "duration_ms": 367713, "execution_mode": "blueprint_chain_of_thought", "input": "Assess the suitability and network context of station MTA1 based on the completed profile of MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv (50.4 MB; 250,000 rows; all 8 required columns present; 5,000-row sample profiled with scan-limited statistics available: ~1 second cadence observed, displacement ranges profiled, uncertainty components present, zero nulls in sample). Evaluate MTA1's network positioning, station spacing, coverage, and analytical fitness within the Los Angeles region's 72-station GNSS catalog (including ranked candidates: MTA1, PKRD, ELSC, USC2, SILK, and others). Provide network-level suitability assessment to support downstream visualization and synthesis.\n\nParent evidence available for this delegated task:\n\n**GNSS Time-Series Profile \u2014 MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv**\n\n**File and Column Inventory:**\n- **Staged path:** D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\n- **File size:** 50.4 MB (50,424,246 bytes)\n- **Total rows in file:** 250,000\n- **Profiling scope:** 5,000 rows (2% sample cap)\n- **Columns (all required present):** time (integer, millisecond epoch), east (float, m), north (float, m), up (float, m), sigEE (float, m), sigNN (float, m), sigUU (float, m), qChannel (integer)\n\n**Time Range and Cadence (Profiled Sample Only):**\n- **Earliest epoch (sample):** 1733184000000 ms\n- **Latest epoch (sample):** 1733189070000 ms\n- **Sample span:** ~5,070 seconds (~84.5 minutes)\n- **Observed cadence (sample):** ~1 second (1000 ms between consecutive rows in visible sample)\n- **Caveat:** Time range and cadence reflect profiled sample only; full-file duration, continuity, and gap characteristics not verified\n\n**Displacement Component Statistics (Profiled 5,000 Rows):**\n- **East:** min = \u22120.07 m, max = \u22120.03 m, mean = \u22120.0472 m\n- **North:** min = 0.029 m, max = 0.058 m, mean = 0.0453 m\n- **Up:** min = 0.051 m, max = 0.224 m, mean = 0.1358 m\n- **Caveat:** These are descriptive statistics of the profiled sample; ranges alone do not establish signal quality or noise characteristics\n\n**Uncertainty Component Ranges (Profiled 5,000 Rows):**\n- **sigEE (East uncertainty):** min = 0.032 m, max = 0.035 m, mean = 0.0334 m\n- **sigNN (North uncertainty):** min = 0.032 m, max = 0.036 m, mean = 0.0330 m\n- **sigUU (Up uncertainty):** min = 0.062 m, max = 0.066 m, mean = 0.0651 m\n- **qChannel (quality flag):** min = 1314021, max = 2411021, mean = 1847152 (integer codes; no decoded interpretation available)\n- **Caveat:** Uncertainty values are descriptive statistics; no explicit noise thresholds or suitability-for-analysis criteria applied\n\n**Data Completeness (Profiled Sample):**\n- **Missing values:** 0 (zero nulls across all 8 columns in 5,000 profiled rows)\n- **Row continuity (sample):** No gaps in 1-second cadence across visible epochs\n- **Caveat:** Missing-value status assessed for profiled rows only; full-file missing-value occurrence not verified\n\n**Analysis Limitations:**\n- Numeric summaries (row statistics, time range, cadence, missing-value count) derived from 5,000-row sample (2% of 250,000 total file); full-file characteristics not verified\n- Full-file duration, continuity, large data gaps, and outlier extent cannot be assessed from sample profile alone\n- Cadence and completeness observations are sample-only; full-file cadence regularity not verified\n- Uncertainty columns are populated; values are descriptive statistics, not fitness-for-analysis certificates\n- Quality flag (qChannel) numeric codes provided; no interpretation or threshold-based quality assessment applied\n\n**Status:** GNSS profile complete. Station/network suitability assessment pending.\n\nAccumulated typed workflow state from prior CLIO tool evidence (authoritative; use this before local prose summaries):\n{\"workflow_state\": {\"acquisition\": {\"analysis_ready\": true, \"local_path\": \"D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"metadata_path\": \"D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv\", \"metadata_source_url\": \"https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv\", \"size_bytes\": 50424246, \"source_url\": \"https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"status\": \"staged\"}, \"catalog\": {\"status\": \"metadata_found\"}, \"geospatial\": {\"bbox\": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], \"center_lat\": 34.0536909, \"center_lon\": -118.242766, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"provenance\": \"osm_nominatim\", \"radius_km\": 50, \"region_name\": \"Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\", \"status\": \"resolved\"}, \"orchestration_stage\": \"analysis_in_progress\", \"pipeline_required\": [\"geospatial\", \"data\", \"analysis\", \"visualization\", \"synthesis\"], \"profile\": {\"cadence_observed_seconds\": 1, \"columns\": [\"time\", \"east\", \"north\", \"up\", \"sigEE\", \"sigNN\", \"sigUU\", \"qChannel\"], \"columns_status\": \"all_required_present\", \"displacement_components\": {\"east\": {\"max\": -0.03, \"mean\": -0.0472, \"min\": -0.07, \"unit\": \"m\"}, \"north\": {\"max\": 0.058, \"mean\": 0.0453, \"min\": 0.029, \"unit\": \"m\"}, \"up\": {\"max\": 0.224, \"mean\": 0.1358, \"min\": 0.051, \"unit\": \"m\"}}, \"limitations\": [\"Numeric summaries derived from 5,000-row sample (2% of 250,000 total); full-file characteristics not verified\", \"Time range reflects profiled sample only; full-file duration unknown\", \"Cadence observed in sample; full-file continuity and gaps not verified\", \"Missing-value status assessed for profiled rows only; full-file missing-value occurrence unknown\", \"Uncertainty values are descriptive statistics; no explicit noise thresholds or suitability criteria applied\"], \"missing_values\": {\"count\": 0, \"scope\": \"profiled_rows_5000_only\"}, \"rows_profiled\": 5000, \"rows_scanned\": 250000, \"scan_limited\": true, \"status\": \"complete\", \"time_range_profiled_ms\": {\"max\": 1733189070000, \"min\": 1733184000000, \"span_seconds\": 5070}, \"uncertainty_components\": {\"qChannel\": {\"max\": 2411021, \"mean\": 1847152, \"min\": 1314021, \"note\": \"integer codes; no decoded interpretation available\"}, \"sigEE\": {\"max\": 0.035, \"mean\": 0.0334, \"min\": 0.032, \"unit\": \"m\"}, \"sigNN\": {\"max\": 0.036, \"mean\": 0.033, \"min\": 0.032, \"unit\": \"m\"}, \"sigUU\": {\"max\": 0.066, \"mean\": 0.0651, \"min\": 0.062, \"unit\": \"m\"}}}, \"request_scope\": \"full_pipeline\", \"resource_candidate\": {\"geographically_grounded\": true, \"station_id\": \"MTA1\", \"status\": \"selected\"}, \"station_catalog\": {\"candidate_count\": 72, \"station_ids\": [\"MTA1\", \"PKRD\", \"ELSC\", \"USC2\", \"SILK\", \"OXYC\", \"P800\", \"LEE2\", \"LEEP\", \"GVRS\", \"BGIS\", \"NOPK\", \"MHMS\", \"VDCY\", \"CIT1\", \"MILK\", \"BRAN\", \"P799\", \"HOLP\", \"LFRS\", \"DYH2\", \"WNRA\", \"BKMS\", \"JPLM\", \"FCTF\", \"UCLP\", \"WRHS\", \"RHCL\", \"WHC1\", \"CSDH\", \"RHCG\", \"LONG\", \"CRHS\", \"WLSN\", \"VIMT\", \"LBC1\", \"LPHS\", \"WMAP\", \"TORP\", \"LBCH\", \"LBC2\", \"HBCO\", \"WCHS\", \"CVHS\", \"PVRS\", \"SNHS\", \"PVHS\", \"AZU1\", \"CGDM\", \"LAPC\", \"CSN1\", \"DAM3\", \"DAM2\", \"BLSA\", \"VNCX\", \"P517\", \"P587\", \"CMP9\", \"CBHS\", \"SPMS\", \"CHIL\", \"SPK1\", \"PVE3\", \"VTIS\", \"PSDM\", \"CCCS\", \"ROCK\", \"LORS\", \"SACY\", \"SKYB\", \"TWMS\", \"CLAR\"], \"status\": \"ranked\"}, \"user_geography\": \"Los Angeles\"}}", "output": "**Station MTA1 Preliminary Network Suitability Assessment**\n\n**Geographic and Catalog Context:**\n- MTA1 is the selected primary station candidate for Los Angeles region (center: 34.053\u00b0N, \u2212118.243\u00b0W; bounding box: \u2212118.668\u00b0 to \u2212118.155\u00b0 lon, 33.660\u00b0 to 34.337\u00b0 lat).\n- Ranked within a 72-station GNSS catalog including candidates PKRD, ELSC, USC2, SILK, OXYC, and 66 additional stations.\n- Geographic grounding: confirmed.\n\n**Data Profile Summary (Sample-Based):**\n- **File**: 50.4 MB; 250,000 total rows.\n- **Profiling Scope**: 5,000 rows (2% sample-limited cap).\n- **Column Status**: All 8 required columns present (time, east, north, up, sigEE, sigNN, sigUU, qChannel).\n- **Missing Values (Profiled Sample)**: 0 nulls detected across 5,000 rows (scope: profiled rows only; full-file missing-value status not verified).\n\n**Time and Cadence (Sample Observed Only):**\n- Profiled time range: ~5,070 seconds (~84.5 minutes).\n- Cadence observed in sample: ~1 second between consecutive epochs.\n- **Caveat**: Full-file duration, cadence regularity, and gap characteristics not verified.\n\n**Displacement Component Ranges (Profiled 5,000 Rows):**\n- East: \u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m (mean: \u22120.0472 m)\n- North: 0.029 to 0.058 m (mean: 0.0453 m)\n- Up: 0.051 to 0.224 m (mean: 0.1358 m)\n- **Note**: These are descriptive ranges; displacement statistics do not establish signal quality or noise characteristics in isolation.\n\n**Uncertainty Components (Centimeter-Scale):**\n- **sigEE (East)**: 0.032\u20130.035 m (mean: 0.0334 m) \u2014 ~3.3 cm centimeter-scale\n- **sigNN (North)**: 0.032\u20130.036 m (mean: 0.033 m) \u2014 ~3.3 cm centimeter-scale\n- **sigUU (Up)**: 0.062\u20130.066 m (mean: 0.0651 m) \u2014 ~6.5 cm centimeter-scale\n- **qChannel**: 1314021\u20132411021 (integer flag; no decoded interpretation available)\n- **Assessment**: Centimeter-level horizontal and vertical uncertainties are populated. These numeric summaries are not fitness-for-analysis certificates; no explicit noise thresholds or analytical-fitness criteria are applied.\n\n**Network Suitability Determination:**\n- **Single-Station Adequacy**: MTA1 meets data staging and column inventory requirements. Geographic positioning within the Los Angeles region is confirmed. Sample-level data continuity (zero missing values, consistent ~1-second cadence in visible epochs) supports preliminary staging readiness.\n- **Multi-Station Considerations**: Network-level station spacing, coverage gaps, and inter-station cross-validation requirements are not addressed in current evidence. Downstream visualization and synthesis should evaluate whether MTA1 alone provides sufficient spatial coverage or whether a multi-station fanout (e.g., to PKRD, ELSC, USC2) is necessary for regional confidence, network redundancy, or deformation-pattern triangulation.\n\n**Analytical Fitness (Preliminary):**\n- Column inventory: complete.\n- Geographic grounding: confirmed.\n- Centimeter-scale uncertainties: present and quantified (not sub-centimeter).\n- Sample-level continuity: no missing values in profiled 5,000 rows.\n- **Full-file verification pending**: Duration, gap structure, cadence regularity, outlier extent, and complete missing-value assessment require full-file profiling.\n- **Quality assessment**: qChannel numeric range available; decoded interpretation not available. Quality flag status assessed descriptively only.\n\n**Conclusion:**\nMTA1 is a **geographically grounded, preliminary candidate** meeting data inventory and column completeness requirements. Centimeter-scale uncertainty components and sample-observed ~1-second cadence support staging. **Full-file temporal characteristics, noise baselines, and gap-free verification are required for downstream analysis fitness certification.** Network-level integration (distance to PKRD, ELSC, USC2, and others; inter-station spacing) should inform multi-station validation strategy. Current assessment is at the level of column/range review and geographic positioning; further refinement of temporal continuity, analytical fitness, and network coverage fit requires complete-file analysis and comparative station-pair evaluation.", "output_summary": "**Station MTA1 Preliminary Network Suitability Assessment**\n\n**Geographic and Catalog Context:**\n- MTA1 is the selected primary station candidate for Los Angeles region (center: 34.053\u00b0N, \u2212118.243\u00b0W; bounding box: \u2212118.668\u00b0 to \u2212118.155\u00b0 lon, 33.660\u00b0 to 34.337\u00b0 lat).\n- Ranked within a 72-station GNSS catalog including candidates PKRD, ELSC, USC2, SILK, OXYC, and 66 additional stations.\n- Geographic grounding: confirmed.\n\n**Data Profile Summary (Sample-Based):**\n- **File**: 50.4 MB; 250,000 total rows.\n- **Profiling Scope**: 5,000 rows (2% sample-limited cap).\n- **Column Status**: All 8 required columns present (time, east, north, up, sigEE, sigNN, sigUU, qChannel).\n- **Missing Values (Profiled Sample)**: 0 nulls detected across 5,000 rows (scope: profiled rows only; full-file missing-value status not verified).\n\n**Time and Cadence (Sample Observed Only):**\n- Profiled time range: ~5,070 seconds (~84.5 minutes).\n- Cadence observed in sample: ~1 second between consecutive epochs.\n- **Caveat**: Full-file duration, cadence regularity, and gap characteristics not verified.\n\n**Displacement Component Ranges (Profiled 5,000 Rows):**\n- East: \u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m (mean: \u22120.0472 m)\n- North: 0.029 to 0.058 m (mean: 0.0453 m)\n- Up: 0.051 to 0.224 m (mean: 0.1358 m)\n- **Note**: These are descriptive ranges; displacement statistics do not establish signal quality or noise characteristics in isolation.\n\n**Uncertainty Components (Centimeter-Scale):**\n- **sigEE (East)**: 0.032\u20130.035 m (mean: 0.0334 m) \u2014 ~3.3 cm centimeter-scale\n- **sigNN (North)**: 0.032\u20130.036 m (mean: 0.033 m) \u2014 ~3.3 cm centimeter-scale\n- **sigUU (Up)**: 0.062\u20130.066 m (mean: 0.0651 m) \u2014 ~6.5 cm centimeter-scale\n- **qChannel**: 1314021\u20132411021 (integer flag; no decoded interpretation available)\n- **Assessment**: Centimeter-level horizontal and vertical uncertainties are populated. These numeric summaries are not fitness-for-analysis certificates; no explicit noise thresholds or analytical-fitness criteria are applied.\n\n**Network Suitability Determination:**\n- **Single-Station Adequacy**: MTA1 meets data staging and column inventory requirements. Geographic positioning within the Los Angeles region is confirmed. Sample-level data continuity (zero missing values, consistent ~1-second cadence in visible epochs) supports preliminary staging readiness.\n- **Multi-Station Considerations**: Network-level station spacing, coverage gaps, and inter-station cross-validation requirements are not addressed in current evidence. Downstream visualization and synthesis should evaluate whether MTA1 alone provides sufficient spatial coverage or whether a multi-station fanout (e.g., to PKRD, ELSC, USC2) is necessary for regional confidence, network redu