": 0.033, "min": 0.032, "unit": "m"}, "sigUU": {"max": 0.066, "mean": 0.0651, "min": 0.062, "unit": "m"}}}}, "children": [{"delegate_to": "gnss_timeseries_analysis", "agent_id": "gnss_timeseries_analysis", "question": "Profile the staged MTA1 GNSS CSV at D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv. Extract and report: (1) column names and required fields (time, east/north/up displacement, uncertainty columns); (2) total rows and rows examined in scan; (3) time range (earliest and latest epoch timestamps); (4) sample cadence (interval between consecutive epochs); (5) displacement component statistics (east/north/up: min, max, mean values if available); (6) uncertainty/error column ranges and numeric summaries; (7) missing-value counts and scope; (8) any data completeness observations. Scan the full file or a representative sample proportional to file size.", "thought": "The staged acquisition confirms `analysis_ready=true` with a verified local path to the MTA1 station CSV (50.4 MB). The user explicitly requests a time-series profile report: time range, cadence, row statistics, and displacement statistics (east/north/up components). This is the core domain of the `gnss_timeseries_analysis` expert, which owns the `pandas_profile_csv` tool and can extract these characteristics from the staged CSV. No seismic event catalog is requested at this stage, and station network suitability assessment can follow once the profile evidence is grounded. I will route to the profiling child first and await its typed evidence before proceeding.", "status": "completed", "execute": true, "source": "agent_next_expert", "parent_id": "analysis", "pack_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "provider_id": "", "model_id": "", "fallback_warnings": [], "stage": "delegate.completed", "delegation_lifecycle": "sync", "return_to": "analysis", "depth": 0, "duration_ms": 79533, "execution_mode": "blueprint_react", "input": "Profile the staged MTA1 GNSS