eseries.png` (absolute path in workspace root)\n\nI'll use the default title and max_rows settings since the instructions indicate calling the function with explicit parameters for the core arguments.\n\nThe output file should be station-named with a `.png` extension in the same directory as the staged CSV. I have the profiling information already available in the workflow state, so I know the exact column names to use. The three displacement components need to be plotted against the time column, and I'll place the output in the workspace root directory. The output path completes to `D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\MTA1_displacement_timeseries.png`. All path escaping is correct for the JSON format\u2014backslashes are properly doubled. The tool arguments are ready with the profiled data path, time column for the x-axis, the three displacement components for the y-axes, and the output filename for the PNG artifact."}}

