ojects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\MTA1_displacement_timeseries\"\n\nThe profiling shows displacement measurements across three axes: eastward motion between -0.07 and -0.03 meters, northward between 0.029 and 0.058 meters, and vertical between 0.051 and 0.224 meters. No missing values were detected in the 5000 profiled rows, with measurement uncertainty ranging from 3 to 7 centimeters. A displacement timeseries visualization has been generated and stored locally. & provenance limitations \u2014 I need to be straightforward about what this analysis actually covers. The profile is based on 5,000 rows, so I can't claim full temporal coverage. Temporal continuity hasn't been verified. The scan is limited, which means gaps could exist in the data. I should note that data_blocked is false, confirming the CSV staged successfully at \"D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\". The station_id \"MTA1\" matches both the filename and the resource candidate. I won't convert rows_scanned into cadence since I already have cadence_observed_seconds. I'll use the exact paths from the workflow_state and avoid citing external sources for region geometry.\n\nThe workflow_state contains acquisition, artifact, profile, and resource_candidate models that I need to echo verbatim. Since this is the synthesis expert running last, the next expert is 'finish' with no additional task. This run successfully traced from geospatial resolution identifying MTA1 as the closest station within 50 km of Los Angeles, through acquisition staging the full 250,000-row dataset from DataCollaboratory, to profiling that scanned a 5,000-row sample revealing displacement patterns. MB, 250,000 rows) sourced from https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv. The profiled sample (5,000 rows, 2% of total) reveals displacement spanning \u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m eastward, 0.029 to 0.058 m northward, and 0.051 to 0.224 m vertically, with ~1-second sampling intervals and no missing values. Measurement uncertainty sits at 3\u20137 cm, with horizontal components around 3.3 cm and vertical around 6.5 cm.\n\nA visualization of the displacement time series (east, north, up components) has been generated at `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1_displacement_timeseries.png`. The full dataset's temporal span, continuity, and internal gaps remain uncharacterized since only a scan-limited sample was analyzed; quality flags like qChannel are present but not yet decoded. This profile confirms data presence and approximate magnitude but requires complete-file analysis to establish full coverage and temporal characteristics.\n\nThe grounded provenance model captures the station identifier (MTA1), file paths, and source URL. The workflow state reflects acquisition readiness with the local CSV path, file size, and upstream source documented. I need to verify the schema requirements more carefully. The models specify exact fields: acquisition_model needs analysis_ready, local_path, size_bytes, source_url, and status; artifact_model requires path and status; profile_model needs rows_scanned and status; resource_candidate_model requires geographically_grounded, station_id, and status. The incoming workflow_state contains additional fields like geospatial coordinates, cadence_observed_seconds, displacement_range_m, and missing_values_count that aren't part of the defined schema. Since the instruction emphasizes a closed schema with only specified fields and explicitly excludes selected_station, candidates, assessment, and next_steps, I should filter the incoming data to include only what's defined in the models. I need to map the upstream values to the schema fields. From the provided workflow_state, I have:\n\nacquisition fields: analysis_ready (true), local_path (\"D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\"), size_bytes (50424246), source_url (\"https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\"), status (\"staged\")\n\nartifact fields: path (\"D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\MTA1_displacement_timeseries.png\"), status (\"ready\")\n\nprofile fields: rows_scanned (250000), status (\"complete\")\n\nresource_candidate fields: geographically_grounded appears to be derived from context as true, station_id (\"MTA1\"), status (\"selected\")\n\nThe schema is closed, so I should only include defined fields and set undefined ones to null. The artifact schema only specifies path and status, so I won't include extra fields like columns or kind even if they appear in the incoming data. I'll construct the output by filling schema-defined fields with their upstream values and leaving unspecified fields as null. The synthesis expert's workflow_state schema is intentionally restrictive with a closed structure, so I'm filtering out extra fields like geospatial metadata and child resources that aren't part of the target model.\n\nLooking at the profile section specifically, the incoming data contains many fields\u2014cadence_observed_seconds, displacement_range_m, missing_values_count, missing_values_scope, rows_profiled, scan_limited, and uncertainty_scale_cm\u2014but the synthesis_workflow_state_profile_model only accepts rows_scanned and status. I need to extract just those two fields for the output.\n\nFor resource_candidate, the upstream state provides distance_km, station_id, and status, but the schema defines geographically_grounded, station_id, and status. I'll keep station_id and status from the incoming data, set geographically_grounded to true since the geospatial resolution succeeded, and drop distance_km since it's not in the schema.\n\nSince this is the synthesis expert running last, the next_expert value is 'finish'\u2014we're done after this step. I need to verify the output format matches the requirements\u2014it should be markdown prose starting