**PNG:** `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1_displacement_timeseries.png` \u2014 time series of east, north, and up displacement components.\n\n## Freshness, coverage & provenance limitations\n\nThe numeric summaries and cadence reflect a 2% scan-limited sample; the full 250,000-row dataset's actual time span, temporal continuity, internal gaps, and complete displacement distribution are not yet characterized. Missing-value assessment applies only to the profiled 5,000 rows. Quality flags (e.g., qChannel) present in the data are not yet decoded. This profile establishes data presence and displacement scale, but full-file coverage assessment requires staged analysis of the complete timeseries.", "expert_handoffs": [], "tools_called": [], "file_diffs": [], "error_info": null, "reasoning": "This is a successful end-to-end run: geospatial resolution identified Los Angeles with center 34.0536909\u00b0N, \u2212118.242766\u00b0W and 50 km radius; station catalog selection ranked MTA1 first among 72 candidates at 0.30 km distance; acquisition staged 250,000 rows from DataCollaboratory; profiling scanned a 5,000-row sample revealing displacement ranges and uncertainty estimates; visualization generated a displacement timeseries PNG. All upstream workflow_state fields are present and grounded in acquisition.status=staged, analysis_ready=true. No child failures were reported. The synthesis merges these into a concise user brief, copying exact paths and station id, preserving grounded numeric evidence, and honestly disclosing the scan-limited profile scope and unverified temporal continuity."}}}

