event: turn.action.added
id: 6335
data: {"type": "turn.action.added", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:17:39.355199+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_041054051c41", "action": {"kind": "return", "call_id": "return:synthesis:main:0", "agent_id": "synthesis", "target_agent": "main", "summary": "## Region\n\nLos Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States \u2014 search centered at 34.0536909\u00b0N, 118.242766\u00b0W with a 50 km search radius (osm_nominatim).\n\n## Station selected\n\nStation **MTA1** \u2014 the closest EarthScope GNSS station in the region, located 0.30 km from the search center and ranked first among 72 candidates in the catalog.\n\n## Data resource\n\n- **Staged CSV:** `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv` (50.4 MB, 250,000 rows)\n- **Source URL:** https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\n\n## Profile evidence\n\nA 5,000-row scan-limited sample (2% of the full dataset) reveals:\n\n- **Displacement ranges** (meters):\n - East: \u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m\n - North: 0.029 to 0.058 m\n - Up: 0.051 to 0.224 m\n- **Cadence:** ~1-second sampling observed in sample\n- **Missing values:** Zero in the 5,000 rows profiled\n- **Uncertainty:** 3\u20137 cm scale (east/north ~3.3 cm, vertical ~6.5 cm)\n\n## Visualization\n\n- **PNG:** `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1_displacement_timeseries.png` \u2014 time series of east, north, and up displacement components.\n\n## Freshness, coverage & provenance limitations\n\nThe numeric summaries and cadence reflect a 2% scan-limited sample; the full 250,000-row dataset's actual time span, temporal continuity, internal gaps, and complete displacement distribution are not yet characterized. Missing-value assessment applies only to the profiled 5,000 rows. Quality flags (e.g., qChannel) present in the data are not yet decoded. This profile establishes data presence and displacement scale, but full-file coverage assessment requires staged analysis of the complete timeseries."}}}

