data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:17:58.149801+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_041054051c41", "message_id": "msg_asst_f80e8e6df00b", "part_id": "part_23ad54630156", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "Let me carefully analyze this request and the returned child expert results.\n\n## Understanding the Context\n\nThe user's original request was:\n\"Find the nearest EarthScope GNSS station to Los Angeles, stage its time-series CSV, profile it, and create a displacement time-series plot.\"\n\nThis is a FULL PIPELINE request that requires:\n1. geospatial resolution (place \u2192 coordinates)\n2. data discovery & staging (station CSV)\n3. analysis (profiling)\n4. visualization (PNG plot)\n5. synthesis (final answer)\n\n## Child Results Review\n\nThe returned child results show:\n\n1. **geospatial**: \u2705 COMPLETED\n   - Resolved Los Angeles to center 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W, 50 km radius\n   - Status: resolved with high confidence\n   - Provenance: osm_nominatim\n\n2. **data**: \u2705 COMPLETED\n   - Discovered 72 EarthScope GNSS stations\n   - Staged the nearest station (MTA1, 0.30 km away)\n   - CSV path: `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n   - Source URL provided\n   - File size: 50.4 MB, 250,000 rows\n   - Required columns present: time, east, north, up \u2705\n   - Status: analysis_ready\n\n3. **analysis**: \u2705 COMPLETED\n   - Profiled 5,000 rows (2% sample-limited cap)\n   - Identified all required columns present\n   - Displacement ranges provided (east, north, up in meters)\n   - Cadence: ~1 second observed\n   - Missing values: 0 in profiled sample\n   - Uncertainty: 3\u20137 cm scale\n   - Full-file characteristics NOT verified (scan-limited)\n   \n4. **visualization**: \u2705 COMPLETED\n   - Generated PNG artifact at `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1_displacement_timeseries.png` showing 2000 sampled points across east, north, and up displacement components with UTC epoch milliseconds on the x-axis.\n\n5. **synthesis**: \u2705 COMPLETED\n   - Assembled final response with region context, station identification, data resource documentation, profiling evidence, visualization artifact, and documented limitations.\n\nThe orchestrator state indicates synthesis is pending, yet the child results show synthesis has already executed and returned its complete output. According to the system instructions, synthesis marks the terminal stage of the pipeline\u2014once it completes, the next action should be `finish`.\n\nI'm now on the turn following synthesis's return. The workflow has accumulated all required evidence through geospatial, data, analysis, visualization, and synthesis stages. I need to set `next_expert=finish`, pass through the synthesis result as my response, maintain the workflow_state with its grounded findings, and leave `next_task` empty since the pipeline is complete.\n\nThe original request has been fulfilled: nearest station identified (MTA1 at 0.30 km), data staged and profiled (5,000 rows with displacement metrics), visualization generated (PNG artifact), and synthesis has provided the final answer with proper citations and limitations noted. I should not regenerate or modify the synthesis output, nor should I re-engage any child experts since all work is done."}, "replay": true}

