data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:18:19.701071+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_617ddf77a4574ab6", "event_type": "expert.response.completed", "session_id": "sess_a6b75b5c73dd", "workspace_id": "ws_ndp_demo", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_041054051c41", "turn_id": "msg_user_041054051c41", "span_id": "sem_617ddf77a4574ab6", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "completed", "summary": "Expert main produced a response.", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:18:19.558531+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "main"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {"agent_blueprint_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "parent_expert": ""}, "provider": {"provider_id": "", "model_id": ""}, "payload": {"selected_expert": "main", "route_source": "agent_blueprint", "route_reason": "Session selected Agent Blueprint expert 'main'.", "answer": "## Region\n\nLos Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States \u2014 search centered at 34.0536909\u00b0N, 118.242766\u00b0W with a 50 km search radius (osm_nominatim).\n\n## Station selected\n\nStation **MTA1** \u2014 the closest EarthScope GNSS station in the region, located 0.30 km from the search center and ranked first among 72 candidates in the catalog.\n\n## Data resource\n\n- **Staged CSV:** `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv` (50.4 MB, 250,000 rows)\n- **Source URL:** https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\n\n## Profile evidence\n\nA 5,000-row scan-limited sample (2% of the full dataset) reveals:\n\n- **Displacement ranges** (meters):\n  - East: \u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m\n  - North: 0.029 to 0.058 m\n  - Up: 0.051 to 0.224 m\n- **Cadence:** ~1-second sampling observed in sample\n- **Missing values:** Zero in the 5,000 rows profiled\n- **Uncertainty:** 3\u20137 cm scale (east/north ~3.3 cm, vertical ~6.5 cm)\n\n## Visualization\n\n- **PNG:** `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1_displacement_timeseries.png` \u2014 time series of east, north, and up displacement components.\n\n## Freshness, coverage & provenance limitations\n\nThe numeric summaries and cadence reflect a 2% scan-limited sample; the full 250,000-row dataset's actual time span, temporal continuity, internal gaps, and complete displacement distribution are not yet characterized. Missing-value assessment applies only to the profiled 5,000 rows. Quality flags (e.g., qChannel) present in the data are not yet decoded. This profile establishes data presence and displacement scale, but full-file coverage assessment requires staged analysis of the complete timeseries.", "expert_handoffs": [], "tools_called": [], "file_diffs": [], "error_info": null, "reasoning": "All five stages of the requested pipeline have completed and returned grounded evidence:\n\n1. **geospatial** resolved Los Angeles to center 34.0536909\u00b0N, 118.242766\u00b0W (50 km radius, osm_nominatim).\n2. **data** discovered 72 stations and staged the nearest (MTA1, 0.30 km away) with full CSV path and source URL.\n3. **analysis** profiled the 250,000-row staged CSV, scanning 5,000 rows (2% sample-limited cap), and reported displacement ranges, ~1-second cadence, zero missing values in profiled sample, and 3\u20137 cm uncertainty scale.\n4. **visualization** rendered the PNG plot artifact (`MTA1_displacement_timeseries.png`) with east, north, up displacement components across 2,000 plotted points.\n5. **synthesis** has already written the final user-facing answer, merging region, station, staged resource, profile evidence, artifact path, and explicit limitations (scan-limited profile; full-file characteristics not verified).\n\nPer the system instructions: \"*`next_expert=finish` is valid ONLY after `synthesis` has run \u2014 `synthesis` is ALWAYS the last child, and you finish on the turn AFTER it returns, carrying its answer.*\"\n\nSynthesis has completed and returned a final answer. I am now on the turn after synthesis returned. All claims in the synthesis answer are backed by child-returned evidence in the accumulated workflow_state. No re-delegation is needed."}}, "replay": true}

